INSERT INTO surveys (id, vessel_id, surveyor_id, broker_id, surveyor_name, condition_type, status, form_status, location, date_of_survey, due_date, concern_from_surveyor, resume_from_surveyor, summary, policy_period_start, policy_period_end, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (121, 66, 1, 9, 'Junor Maulana Ahmad', 'Survey', 'Cancelled', 'complete', 'Sorong Port, West Papua', '2024-09-23', '2024-10-11', '<p class="MsoNormal">The safety equipment such as oil absorbent and scupper plugsrnshould be provided onboard the vessel. The charts should be provided with thernlatest update. The doubling in cargo hold no.1 and internal condition of ballastrntank no. 1 should be renewed.</p>', '<p>At the time of our survey, we were unable to see the overall condition of the vessel''s hull due to the vessel was lying berthed at the port. As far as we could ascertain, the structural condition of the vessel was generally in good condition, with good painting work and spot indentation sighted at several places. The condition of the port side draft mark and load lines were clearly marked. Generally, the deck plating on the forecastle, main, and poop deck was found in fair condition. The emergency fire hose test was available for our inspection and found in satisfactory condition.</p><p>The navigational and communication equipment was sufficient for domestic local trading areas within Indonesian waters. Also, the machinery equipment was found in fair and satisfactory condition during our inspection.</p><p>Nevertheless, the crew''s skill in working and operating the vessel was considered sufficient, and they were familiar with the type and size of the vessel.</p><div><br></div>', '<p class="MsoNormal">SUMMARY</p><p class="MsoNormal">The survey onboard MV "LINTAS BAHARI INDONESIA"rnwas carried out on 23 September 2024 at Sorong, West Papua, with attendance:</p><p class="MsoNormal">1.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Yohanis -rnMaster of the vessel<o:p></o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal">2.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; PriyornKaryudi - Chief Officer of the vessel<o:p></o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal">3.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; ArkanrnAbdul Afif - Second Officer of the vessel<o:p></o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal">4.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Budiyantorn- Chief Engineer of the vessel<o:p></o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal">5.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; PangesturnNugroho - Second Engineer of the vessel<o:p></o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal">6.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Riyando AndirnSifano - Third Engineer of the vessel<o:p></o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal">MV "LINTAS BAHARI INDONESIA" is a 610 GT generalrncargo vessel presently owned and operated by PT. Mandala Sejahtera Abadi. Atrnthe time of our survey, the vessel was lying berthed at Rakyat Port, Sorong,rnWest Papua.<o:p></o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal">VESSEL CERTIFICATION AND DOCUMENTATION</p><p class="MsoNormal">Class survey records for hull and machinery were madernavailable at the time of the survey. The class is maintained. In the meantime,rnthe statutory certificate was in valid condition and not overdue from the nextrninspection schedule or renewal.</p><p class="MsoNormal">The latest UT thickness measurement report was madernavailable and is in our possession after we disembarked from the vessel. Thernvessel''s steel structures'' diminution level is still below the class maximumrnallowable limit of 20%.<o:p></o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal">GENERAL CONDITION OF HULL AND DECK</p><p class="MsoNormal">As far as could be ascertained, the port and starboard sidernshell plating from aft to fore-ends, was visually found in fair condition, andrnfair painting works with light indentation were sighted at places. The portsiderndraft mark and load lines were clearly marked and visible.</p><p class="MsoNormal">At our attendance, the visible condition of the deck platingrnon the forecastle, main, and poop deck was found in fair condition. The portrnand starboard bulwark and railing on the forecastle, main, poop, andrnaccommodation deck were found in order.</p><p class="MsoNormal">The mooring equipment, which is double bollards and capstan,rnwas found in fair condition, with the safe working load information. Most airrnvents and sounding pipes were also clearly marked with the compartment theyrnserve. The watertight door and booby hatch leading to the engine room werernfound in fair condition with a good rubber seal.</p><p class="MsoNormal">The winch and windlass are generally in fair condition andrngood operation. Therefore, the mooring work area was clean and dry on thernforecastle deck.</p><p class="MsoNormal">At the time of our survey, the hatch cover pontoon of thernvessel was found in fair condition with slightly rusted. The internal conditionrnof the cargo hold was found clean and dry while the cargo hold steel structurernincluding the frames and toe bracket was slightly dented and found doublers atrnthe tank top. The suction test using the bilge pump on the cargo hold bilgesrnwas carried out at the time of our survey, and it was found in order whenrntested.</p><p class="MsoNormal">The inspected ballast tanks No. 1P and 1S were found in poorrncondition and wasted in several places. The zinc anode was not sighted on therninspected ballast tanks. However, the ballast tanks pressure test could not berncarried out at the time of our survey.<o:p></o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal">BRIDGE AND NAVIGATION</p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify">The navigation and communicationrnequipment were in good condition when tested and considered sufficient forrndomestic or local trading within Indonesian waters.&nbsp;<span style="font-size: 0.875rem;">The updated NTM (IndonesianrnNotice to Mariners) was available onboard. The nautical publications and chartsrnwere not updated. Meanwhile, the deck logbook was filled out properly by therncrew.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify">The changeover instructions forrnemergency steering were available and posted on the bridge.<o:p></o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal">MACHINERY SPACE AND STEERING GEAR</p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify">The vessel has 1 (one) mainrnengine, 3 (three) auxiliary engines as registered on the class certificate, and 1rn(one) generator set. The Chief Engineer verbally advised that severalrnmachinery equipment testing records were available onboard. The engine logbookrnwas sighted and found to be regularly updated.</p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify">The emergency steering gear andrngenerator were in good order when tested and provided with emergencyrnprocedures.</p><p class="MsoNormal"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal">SAFETY AND OIL POLLUTION PREVENTION</p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify">The safety equipment was found tornbe in order. Sufficient numbers of life jackets were provided on board. 1 (one)rnlifeboat and 4 (four) life rafts were available on board. Portable firernextinguishers were in good condition and regularly serviced. The emergency firernpump test was available for our inspection and found in satisfactory condition.</p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify">The vessel was provided with thernSOPEP box or locker with sufficient SOPEP equipment except oil absorbent.</p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify">The bunkering connection wasrnfound in good condition, and save-all was installed in the surrounding area.rnHowever, most air vents and sounding pipes were clearly marked with therncompartment they serve. The scupper plugs were not available onboard.<o:p></o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p><p>rnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrnrn</p><p class="MsoNormal">== END ==<o:p></o:p></p>', '2024-09-11', '2025-09-11', NOW(), NOW()) ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET status = EXCLUDED.status, summary = EXCLUDED.summary;
INSERT INTO surveys (id, vessel_id, surveyor_id, broker_id, surveyor_name, condition_type, status, form_status, location, date_of_survey, due_date, concern_from_surveyor, resume_from_surveyor, summary, policy_period_start, policy_period_end, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (128, 106, 8, NULL, 'Capt. Andyka D. Paksi', 'Survey', 'Completed', 'complete', 'Tabanio, Tanah Laut Regency, South Kalimantan, Indonesia', '2024-05-28', '2024-03-05', '<p>-</p>', '<p>-</p>', '<p>-</p>', '2024-02-04', '2025-02-04', NOW(), NOW()) ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET status = EXCLUDED.status, summary = EXCLUDED.summary;
INSERT INTO surveys (id, vessel_id, surveyor_id, broker_id, surveyor_name, condition_type, status, form_status, location, date_of_survey, due_date, concern_from_surveyor, resume_from_surveyor, summary, policy_period_start, policy_period_end, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (129, 56, 1, 9, 'Alifian Aji Santoso', 'Survey', 'Completed', 'complete', 'Biringkassi, South Sulawesi', '2024-11-09', '2024-11-27', '<p><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41);">The gyro compass was found out of order and should be repaired. The SOPEP locker, complete with its contents (sawdust, oil dispersant, oil absorbent, fabric), to be provided on board. The scupper plugs should also be provided on board the vessel.</span></p><p>The rubber seals&nbsp;<span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">on the hatch cover were found to be partially detached and should be fixed.<br><br></span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41);">The internal of ballast tanks No. 3S and 3P are generally corroded, and the associated zinc anodes were found fully depleted should be renewed.</span></p>', '<p>The structural condition of the general cargo was found generally in fair condition with fair paintwork. Spot indentation and scratches were found at places. The draft mark and load lines were clearly marked and visible. The deck plating on the forecastle, main, and poop decks were found to be in fair condition.<br><br>The fuel air vent, ventilation pipe, and sounding pipe were marked with the compartment they serve. The hatch cover was the folding type and covered by tarpaulins as a securing device. In addition, the rubber seals on the hatch cover were found to be partially detached.</p><p>The navigation and communication equipment was considered sufficient for domestic local trading areas with Indonesian waters. However, the gyro compass was found out of order.<br><br>The emergency generator and emergency steering gear were found to be in order when tested, and the ballast tank pressure was satisfactory when tested.</p><p>The SOPEP locker, complete with its contents, wasn''t available on board.<br><br>Nevertheless, the crew''s skill in working and operating the general cargo was considered sufficient, and they were familiar with the type and size of the vessel.</p>', '<p><b><u>SUMMARY</u></b></p><p>The survey on board general cargo "PRIMA SAMUDRA" was conducted on 09 November 2024 at the Biringkassi, Pangkep, South Sulawesi, Indonesia with attendance:<br><br>1. Mohammad Fajar Siddiq Arna&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Master of the vessel</p><p>2. Heti Yunisari&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-&nbsp; &nbsp; Chief Officer of the vessel</p><p>3. Kamaruddin&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp; -&nbsp; &nbsp; Second Officer of the vessel</p><p>4. Sugiyanto&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp; -&nbsp; &nbsp; Chief Engineer of the vessel</p><p>5. Alip Saputro&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp; -&nbsp; &nbsp; Second Engineer of the vessel</p><p><br></p><p>General cargo "PRIMA SAMUDRA" is a 1,513 GT presently owned by&nbsp;PT Anugerah Lintas Samudera Raya and operated by PT Vien Fadilah Mutiara, Makassar, South Sulawesi. The vessel has been anchored at the Biringkassi anchorage, South Sulawesi, Indonesia, while waiting for instruction from the shore office for loading the cargo. Furthermore, the vessel''s trading area is in Indonesian waters.</p><p><br></p><p><u><b>VESSEL CERTIFICATION AND DOCUMENTATION</b></u></p><p>Class survey records for hull and machinery were made available at the time of the survey. The class status is maintained. In the meantime, the statutory certificate was in valid condition and not overdue from the next inspection schedule or renewal.<br><br>The&nbsp;<span style="font-size: 0.875rem;">thickness measurement (UTM) report was not available on board the vessel. Later, based on the provided ultrasonic thickness measurement report from the shore office, the diminution level of the vessel steel structures was still below the class maximum allowable limit of 20%.</span></p><p><span style="font-size: 0.875rem;"><br></span></p><p><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><u>GENERAL CONDITION OF HULL AND DECK</u></span><u><b></b></u></p><p>As far as could be ascertained, the starboard and port side shell plating from aft to fore-ends, from sheer down to the waterline, was visually found in fair condition without doublers, fair painting works with light indentation and scratches at places. The draft mark and load lines were clearly marked and visible.</p><p>At our attendance, the visible condition of the deck plating on the forecastle, main, and poop deck was found to be in fair condition. The starboard and port bulwark, railing on the forecastle, main, and poop deck were found in order.</p><p>The mooring equipment, which is a double bollard, capstan, and roller, was found in fair condition complete with the mark of safe working load information. The fuel air vent,&nbsp;<span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">ventilation pipe, and sounding pipe are also marked with the compartment they serve.&nbsp;</span><font color="#212529"><span style="font-size: 0.875rem;">The watertight door was found </span>to be in order, complete with the rubber sealing<span style="font-size: 0.875rem;">.</span></font></p><p style=""><font color="#212529">The hatch cover was the folding type and covered by tarpaulins as a securing device.&nbsp;<span style="font-size: 0.875rem;">The rubber seals on the hatch cover were found to be partially detached. The winch and windlass are generally in fair condition and good operation, complete with save-alls.&nbsp;</span></font><span style="font-size: 0.875rem;">During our attendance, the vessel was empty. The vessel was fitted with 1 (one) cargo hold.</span></p><p style=""><span style="font-size: 0.875rem;"><br></span></p><p style=""><b><u>BALLAST TANKS</u></b></p><p style="">The inspected internal condition of the ballast tanks was found to be generally corroded. Meanwhile, the associated zinc anode was found fully depleted in the internal of ballast tanks No. 3S and 3P.</p><p style="box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 1rem; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Roboto; font-size: 14px; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; white-space: normal; text-decoration-thickness: initial; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial;"><br></p><p style="box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 1rem; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Roboto; font-size: 14px; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; white-space: normal; text-decoration-thickness: initial; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial;"><b><u>BRIDGE DECK NAVIGATION</u></b></p><p style="box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 1rem; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Roboto; font-size: 14px; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; white-space: normal; text-decoration-thickness: initial; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial;">The navigation and communication equipment were found to be in good condition when tested and were considered sufficient for the domestic&nbsp;local trading area within Indonesian waters. However, the gyro compass was found out of order.<br><br>The updated Indonesia Notice to Marine (NTM) was available onboard. The last NTM on the vessel is 08 November 2024. The vessel was provided with updated charts and bridge management records. The deck logbook was generally updated.</p><p style="box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 1rem; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Roboto; font-size: 14px; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; white-space: normal; text-decoration-thickness: initial; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial;"><br></p><p style="box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 1rem; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Roboto; font-size: 14px; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; white-space: normal; text-decoration-thickness: initial; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial;"><b><u>MACHINERY SPACE AND STEERING GEAR</u></b></p><p style="">The vessel is provided with 1 (one) main engine, 3 (three) auxiliary engines, and 2 (two) generator sets which were found in good running condition when tested at the time of our attendance. The auxiliary engines of No.1, 2, and 3 are registered on the class certificate. The engine logbook was sighted and found to be regularly updated.</p><p style="">The emergency steering gear and generator were in good order when tested and provided with emergency procedures.</p><p style=""><br></p><p style=""><u><b>SAFETY AND POLLUTION</b></u></p><p>The vessel was not provided with a SOPEP box complete with its contents (sawdust, oil dispersant, oil absorbent, fabric). The pollution prevention equipment is inadequate in accordance with safety regulations.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>The bunkering connections were found in order complete with save-alls being installed. The fuel air<span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41);">&nbsp;vent, ventilation pipe, and sounding pipe were marked with the compartment they serve.</span>&nbsp;However, the scupper plugs were not available onboard.<br><br>==END==&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p>', '2024-09-27', '2025-09-27', NOW(), NOW()) ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET status = EXCLUDED.status, summary = EXCLUDED.summary;
INSERT INTO surveys (id, vessel_id, surveyor_id, broker_id, surveyor_name, condition_type, status, form_status, location, date_of_survey, due_date, concern_from_surveyor, resume_from_surveyor, summary, policy_period_start, policy_period_end, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (130, 28, 1, 9, 'Alifian Aji Santoso', 'Survey', 'Completed', 'complete', 'Port of Probolinggo, Probolinggo, East Java', '2024-10-29', '2024-10-27', '<p><font color="#212529">The SOPEP locker, complete with its contents (sawdust, oil dispersant, oil absorbent, fabric), weren''t available on board. The scupper plugs should also be provided on board the vessel.</font></p><p><font color="#212529">The save-alls should be provided onboard for the bunkering connections</font><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41);">.</span></p><p>The fuel air vents, ventilation pipe, and sounding pipe should be marked with the compartment they serve, and the bollard should be marked with SWL information.</p><p><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41);">The watertight door should be cropped and renewed due to severe corrosion, and the rubber seal should be fitted and provided onboard.</span></p><p><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">The hatch cover should be cropped and renewed&nbsp;</span>since the hatch cover was wasted in several areas. The rubber seal also showed signs of hardening and missing.</p><p><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41);">The associated zinc anode was found fully depleted in the internal of ballast tanks No. 2S and 2P should be renewed.</span></p>', '<p>The structural condition of the general cargo was found generally in fair condition with fair paintwork. Spot indentation and scratches were found in several places.&nbsp;<span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">The draft mark and load lines were clearly marked and visible.&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">The deck plating on the forecastle, main, and poop decks were found to be in fair condition.&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">The fuel air vent, ventilation pipe, and sounding pipe were not marked with the compartment they serve. In addition,&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">the hatch cover was found to be wasted in several spots. The rubber seal was found missing and hardened.</span></p><p><font color="#212529">The navigational and communication equipment was considered sufficient for domestic local trading areas with Indonesian waters. During our inspection, we found the main engine and auxiliary engines were found in order. Therefore, the emergency generator and emergency steering gear were found to be in order when tested, and the ballast tank pressure was satisfactory when tested.<br><span style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"><br>The SOPEP</span> locker</font><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">, complete with its contents, wasn''t available on board.</span></p><p>Nevertheless, the crew''s skill in working and operating the general cargo was considered sufficient, and they were familiar with the type and size of the vessel.</p>', '<p><font color="#212529"><b><u>SUMMARY</u></b></font></p><p><font color="#212529">The survey on board General Cargo "DORAEMON" was carried out on 29 October 2024 at the port of Probolinggo, Probolinggo, East Java, Indonesia with attendance:</font></p><p><font color="#212529">1. Suripto</font>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Master of the vessel</p><p>2. Sukowandono&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Chief Officer of the vessel</p><p>3. M.Fuad Hasan M&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-&nbsp;&nbsp; Second Officer of the vessel</p><p>4. Yulius Anggoro&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp; -&nbsp; &nbsp;Chief Engineer of the Vessel</p><p>5. Giran&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; -&nbsp; &nbsp;Second Engineer of the vessel</p><p><br></p><p>General cargo "DORAEMON" is a 760 GT presently owned and operated by PT&nbsp;PT SRI MUTIARA ALAM, Probolinggo, East Java. The general cargo has been berthing at the port of Probolinggo, East Java, Indonesia while waiting for instructions from the shore office. Furthermore, the vessel''s trading area is in Indonesian Waters.</p><p><br></p><p><b><u>VESSEL CERTIFICATION AND DOCUMENTATION</u></b></p><p>Class survey records for hull and machinery were made available at the time of the survey. The class status is maintained. In the meantime, the statutory certificate was in valid condition and not overdue from the next inspection schedule or renewal.<br><br>The&nbsp;<span style="font-size: 0.875rem;">thickness measurement (UTM) report was not available on board the vessel. Later, based on the provided ultrasonic thickness measurement report from the shore office, the diminution level of the vessel steel structures was still below the class maximum allowable limit of 20%.</span></p><p><span style="font-size: 0.875rem;"><br></span></p><p><span style="font-size: 0.875rem;"><b><u>GENERAL CONDITION OF HULL AND DECK</u></b></span></p><p>As far as could be ascertained, the starboard and port side shell plating from aft to fore-ends, from sheer down to the waterline, was visually found in fair condition without doublers, and fair painting works with light indentation and scratches at places. T<span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">he draft mark and load lines were clearly marked and visible.</span></p><p><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">At our attendance, the visible condition of the deck plating on the forecastle, main, and poop deck was found in fair condition. The starboard and port bulwark, railing on the forecastle, main, poop, and accommodation deck were found in order.</span></p><p>The mooring equipment, which is a double bollard, capstan, and roller, was found in fair condition, but the safe working load information was not marked. T<span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;"></span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">he fuel air vent, ventilation pipe, and sounding pipe were also not marked with the compartment they serve. The Watertight door</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41);">&nbsp;was found to be severely corroded,&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">and the rubber seal was hardened.</span></p><p><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41);">The hatch cover was found to be wasted in several spots, and t</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41);">he rubber seal was found missing and hardened.</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41);">&nbsp;The winch and windlass are generally in fair condition and good operation complete with save-alls. Therefore, the mooring work area was found clean and dry on the forecastle deck.</span></p><p>During our attendance, the vessel was empty with no cargo. The vessel was fitted with 1 (one) cargo hold. T<span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">he hatch cover was found to be wasted in several spots, and the rubber seal was missing and hardened.</span></p><p><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;"><br></span></p><p><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;"><b><u>BALLAST TANKS</u></b></span></p><p><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41);">The inspected internal condition of the ballast tank was found to be in fair condition and corrosion was sighted at places.</span><br style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41);"><br style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41);"><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41);">Meanwhile, the associated zinc anode was found fully depleted in the internal of ballast tanks No. 2S and 2P.</span></p><p><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41);"><br></span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;"></span></p><p><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;"><b><u>BRIDGE DECK AND NAVIGATION</u></b></span></p><p><font color="#212529">The navigation and communication equipment were in good condition, worked in order when tested, and were considered sufficient for the domestic or local trading area within Indonesian&nbsp;waters. The updated Indonesia Notice to Marine (NTM) was available onboard. The last NTM on the vessel is 18 October 2024.&nbsp;</font><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">The vessel was provided with updated charts and bridge management records. The deck logbook was generally updated.</span></p><p><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;"><br></span></p><p><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;"><b><u>MACHINERY SPACE AND STEERING GEAR</u></b></span></p><p><font color="#212529">The vessel is provided with 1 (one) main engine, 2 (two) auxiliary engines, and 2 (two) generator sets&nbsp;</font><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">which were found in good running condition when tested at the time of our attendance</span><font color="#212529" style="font-size: 0.875rem;">. The a</font><span style="font-size: 0.875rem; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);">uxiliary engines of AE No. 1 and 2 as registered on the class certificate.</span><span style="font-size: 0.875rem; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);">&nbsp;The engine logbook was sighted and found to be regularly updated.</span></p><p><font color="#212529"><br></font>The emergency steering gear and generator were in good order when tested and provided with emergency procedures.</p><p><font color="#212529"><br></font></p><p><font color="#212529"><b><u>SAFETY AND OIL POLLUTION</u></b></font></p><p><font color="#212529">The vessel wasn''t provided with a SOPEP box complete with its contents (</font><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">sawdust, oil dispersant, oil absorbent, fabric). The pollution prevention equipment is inadequate in accordance with safety regulations.</span></p><p><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41);">The bunkering connections were found without save-alls being installed. However, t</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">he fuel air vent, ventilation pipe, and sounding pipe were not marked with the compartment they serve. The scupper plugs were not available onboard.</span></p><p><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;"><br></span></p><p>== END ==</p>', '2024-09-27', '2025-09-27', NOW(), NOW()) ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET status = EXCLUDED.status, summary = EXCLUDED.summary;
