INSERT INTO surveys (id, vessel_id, surveyor_id, broker_id, surveyor_name, condition_type, status, form_status, location, date_of_survey, due_date, concern_from_surveyor, resume_from_surveyor, summary, policy_period_start, policy_period_end, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (495, 395, 1, 9, 'Alifian Aji Santoso', 'Survey', 'Completed', 'complete', 'PT Dok Pantai Lamongan, East Java', '2026-05-25', '2026-05-30', '<p>The safe manning certificates, the officer certificate/ endorsement should be provided onboard. Also the class and statutory certificates should be provided onboard.&nbsp;<span style="font-size: 0.875rem;">The planned maintenance system includes critical equipment, spare parts inventory, overdue maintenance records, and reminders for pending items that should be provided onboard.</span></p><p><span style="font-size: 0.875rem;">The cropped forward starboard side shell should be fitted and renewed. The doubling plates on the boat deck should be cropped and renewed. The mooring works area should be marked with the snapback zone area. The steel structure and internal structure ballast tank Nos. 1P,1S,2P,2S,3P,3S are found wastage at several places should be cropped and renewed. The ballast tank Nos. 1P,1S,2P,2S,3P,3S were found without any zinc anodes and should be installed.</span></p><p>The ship''s lifting equipment and gear maintenance records should be provided on board. The report/records regarding the last maintenance of the main engine should be provided onboard. The manual Calibration result record should be provided onboard. The record for lubricant oil analysis should be provided onboard.&nbsp;</p><p>The engine room was found dirty and slippery should be cleaned. The engine room bilges should be dry and cleaned. The floor plates and ladder were found slippery, should be cleaned.</p><p>The main switchboard indicator and engine indicator should be tested when the vessel is afloat or in normal operation. The store in the engine room was found mesy and should be cleaned. The record for the steering gear testing should be provided. The smoke detector test record should be provided.&nbsp; The main switchboard should be fitted with insulation mats.</p><p>The fire hose lockers was not sufficient in numbers (only had 1 hose locker at the vessel) should be provided following the Fire control plan arrangement. The blackout procedure should be provided on board and posted. The escape route should be clearly marked.&nbsp;</p><p>The voyage stability calculations at the time of departure and on arrival should be calculated and provided onboard. The internal cargo hold 1 was found residue from the recent cargo (cement) that should be cleaned. The bilges at the cargo hold No.1 and 2 should be cleaned.</p>', '<p>The statutory certificate and class certificate were not available onboard at the time of the survey.Â <br class="Apple-interchange-newline"></p><p><span style="font-size: 0.875rem;">The vessel''s structural condition was generally in fair condition, with fair paintwork and light indentations observed at places. However, at the forward starboard side, a cropped plate was found due to the vessel maintenance. The draft marks on the port and starboard sides, as well as the load lines, were clearly marked.</span></p><p>The deck plating on the main bridge deck was found to be in fair condition. However, the doubling plates were found installed at several locations on the boat deck. The emergency fire hose was available on board, but the emergency fire hose locker was not sufficient in numbers (only had 1 (one) hose locker on the 3rd deck).</p><p>The watertight doors were found not fitted with the rubber seal and were wastage at several places on the deck.</p><p>The navigation and communication equipment was sufficient for domestic local trading in Indonesian waters. During our inspection, we found that the machinery equipment was in good working order.</p><div class="qMYqUG_convSearchResultHighlightRoot"><div class="" data-turn-id-container="request-WEB:bc13e477-6513-4580-b322-b377ab72eed3-11" data-is-intersecting="true"><section class="text-token-text-primary w-full focus:outline-none has-data-writing-block:pointer-events-none [&:has([data-writing-block])>*]:pointer-events-auto R6Vx5W_threadScrollVars scroll-mb-[calc(var(--scroll-root-safe-area-inset-bottom,0px)+var(--thread-response-height))] scroll-mt-[calc(var(--header-height)+min(200px,max(70px,20svh)))]" dir="auto" data-turn-id="request-WEB:bc13e477-6513-4580-b322-b377ab72eed3-11" data-turn-id-container="request-WEB:bc13e477-6513-4580-b322-b377ab72eed3-11" data-testid="conversation-turn-24" data-scroll-anchor="false" data-turn="assistant"><div class="text-base my-auto mx-auto pb-10 [--thread-content-margin:var(--thread-content-margin-xs,calc(var(--spacing)*4))] @w-sm/main:[--thread-content-margin:var(--thread-content-margin-sm,calc(var(--spacing)*6))] @w-lg/main:[--thread-content-margin:var(--thread-content-margin-lg,calc(var(--spacing)*16))] px-(--thread-content-margin)"><div class="[--thread-content-max-width:40rem] @w-lg/main:[--thread-content-max-width:48rem] mx-auto max-w-(--thread-content-max-width) flex-1 group/turn-messages focus-visible:outline-hidden relative flex w-full min-w-0 flex-col agent-turn"><div class="flex max-w-full flex-col gap-4 grow"><div data-message-author-role="assistant" data-message-id="00c0f168-66c5-441f-ab96-d52c25103304" dir="auto" data-message-model-slug="gpt-5-5" class="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal outline-none keyboard-focused:focus-ring [.text-message+&]:mt-1" data-turn-start-message="true" tabindex="0"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert wrap-break-word w-full light markdown-new-styling"><blockquote data-start="352" data-end="671" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node=""><p data-start="354" data-end="671" data-is-last-node=""><span data-start="354" data-end="671" data-is-last-node="">Nevertheless, the crew''s ability to work and operate the vessel was considered sufficient, and they appeared familiar with the type and size of the vessel. It should be noted, however, that the crew endorsements could not be verified during the survey as the relevant documents were not made available for review.</span></p></blockquote></div></div></div></div></div></div></section></div></div>', '<p><b><u>SUMMARY</u></b></p><p>The survey onboard General Cargo "SAHABAT PRIMA 8" was carried out on 25 May 2026 at dry dock of PT Dock Pantai Lamongan, Lamongan, East Java, with attendance,</p><p>1. Herlan Satria&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp; - Chief Officer of the General Cargo "SAHABAT PRIMA 8"</p><p>2. Nurul Imam&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;- Chief Engineer of the General Cargo "SAHABAT PRIMA 8"</p><p>3. Peter Hans&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp; - Representative owner of PT Pelayaran Sahabat Karya Abadi</p><p><br></p><p>General cargo "SAHABAT PRIMA 8" is a 2,620 GT vessel presently owned and operated by PT Pelayaran Sahabat Karya Abadi, Jakarta. The vessel has been placed at dry dock of PT Dock Pantai Lamongan, Lamongan, East Java, while commencing the routine maintenance. Furthermore, the vessel''s trading area is mostly in Indonesian waters.</p><p><br></p><p><b><u>VESSEL CERTIFICATION AND DOCUMENTATION</u></b></p><p>Class survey records for hull and machinery were not available at the time of the survey. In the meantime, the statutory certificate was also not available and was not provided by the owner at the time of the survey.</p><p>The latest UT thickness measurement report was available onboard the vessel, and the diminution level of the vessel''s steel structures at several places was found to be below the class maximum allowable limit of 20%.</p><p>The planned maintenance system includes critical equipment, spare parts inventory, overdue maintenance records, and reminders for pending items that should be provided onboard.</p><p><br></p><p><b><u>GENERAL CONDITION OF HULL AND DECK</u></b></p><p>As far as could be ascertained, the port and starboard side shell plating from the aft to the fore-ends was visually in fair condition. However, the forward starboard side shell plate was found cropped due to the vessel''s maintenance at drydock. The painting work is also fair, with some light indentation in places. The draft marks and load lines on both the port and starboard sides were marked and visible.</p><p>During our inspection, the visible condition of the main deck, poopdeck, and bridge deck plating was found to be in fair condition. However, the doubling plates were found installed at several locations on the boat deck. The guard rails, walkways, and ladders on the vessel were found in satisfactory condition.&nbsp;</p><p>The mooring equipment, which includes the double bollard, fairlead, and capstan, was found to be in fair condition however the safe working load information was not clearly marked, and the snap back zone area was not marked. The air sounding pipes and vents were also not clearly marked with the compartments they serve.&nbsp;<span style="font-size: 0.875rem;">The watertight doors were found not fitted with the rubber seal and were wastage at several places.</span></p><p><span style="font-size: 0.875rem;">The winch and windlass as far we could ascertain generally in fair condition. The vessel is equipped with 2 (two) cargo holds.&nbsp;</span><span style="font-size: 0.875rem;">According to the Chief Officer, the vessel is of the single-hull and double-bottom type.</span></p><p>rn</p><p><span style="font-size: 0.875rem;"><b><u>BRIDGE AND NAVIGATION</u></b></span></p><p>The navigation and communication equipment were in good condition when flame tested and were sufficient for domestic or local trading within Indonesian waters. The vessel was equipped with nautical publications, and the bridge management was recorded. The Notice to Marine (NTM) was updated on 22 May 2026. The crew''s emergency steering procedure was provided and posted.</p><p>The deck logbook was generally updated.</p><p><br></p><p><b><u>MACHINERY SPACE AND STEERING GEAR</u></b></p><p>The vessel is equipped with 1 (one) main engine, 2 (two) auxiliary engines, 2 (two) emergency generators, and 1 (one) generator sets, as far we could ascertain, all of which found to be in satisfactory condition. The engine logbook was reviewed and found to be regulary updated. We could not be tested while the vessel was placed at the dry dock.</p><p>The Planned Maintenance System (PMS) was not available onboard. The engine manufacturer''s manual was available onboard.</p><p>The Chief Engineer verbally advised that the vessel was not using the purifier. Due to our inspection, as we could ascertain that by visual the emergency steering gear and generators were in satisfactory condition. We cannot tested due to the vessel being placed at dry dock for routine maintenance. The emergency procedure was available onboard. However, the record testing of the steering test was not available onboard.</p><p><br></p><p><b>SAFETY</b></p><p>The safety equipment was in order. A sufficient number of life jackets were provided onboard. There was 1 (one) lifeboat available. Portable fire extinguishers were in good condition and had been regularly serviced and posted on several places at the Forecastle and engine room. However, the number and arrangement of fire hose lockers were found to be insufficient, with only one (1) fire hose locker available on the 3rd deck, which did not comply with the arrangement shown in the fire Control Plan<span style="font-size: 0.875rem;">.</span></p><p><b><br></b></p><p><b>== END ==</b></p>', '2026-04-30', '2027-04-30', NOW(), NOW()) ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET status = EXCLUDED.status, summary = EXCLUDED.summary;
