font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: " times="" new="" roman";"="">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;n</span></span><!--[endif]--><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size:10.0pt;nmso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;line-height:150%;mso-ansi-language:EN-GB">Internalnstructure of Ballast Tank was found partly rusty &nbsp;</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left:26.9pt;text-indent:-17.85pt;line-height:n150%"><b><u><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size:10.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:9.0pt;nline-height:150%;mso-bidi-font-family:Arial;mso-ansi-language:EN-GB">BridgenManagement.<o:p></o:p></span></u></b></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left:26.9pt;text-indent:-17.85pt;line-height:n150%"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size:10.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:9.0pt;nline-height:150%;mso-bidi-font-family:Arial;mso-ansi-language:EN-GB">Implementednby shipâs crew but still can be improved.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left:26.9pt;text-indent:-17.85pt;line-height:n150%"><b><u><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size:10.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:9.0pt;line-height:150%;mso-bidi-font-family:nArial;mso-ansi-language:EN-GB">Navigational equipment</span></u></b><b><u><span lang="IN" style="font-size:10.0pt;nmso-bidi-font-size:9.0pt;line-height:150%;mso-bidi-font-family:Arial;nmso-ansi-language:IN"><o:p></o:p></span></u></b></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left:8.7pt;text-indent:-8.7pt;line-height:n150%"><span lang="IN" style="font-size:10.0pt;line-height:150%;mso-bidi-font-family:nArial;mso-ansi-language:IN">&nbsp;&nbsp; The </span><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:10.0pt;line-height:150%;mso-bidi-font-family:Arial">navigationnlight was </span><span lang="IN" style="font-size:10.0pt;line-height:150%;nmso-bidi-font-family:Arial;mso-ansi-language:IN">found </span><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:10.0pt;line-height:150%;mso-bidi-font-family:Arial">fitted</span><span lang="IN" style="font-size:10.0pt;line-height:150%;mso-bidi-font-family:Arial;nmso-ansi-language:IN"> on board</span><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:10.0pt;nline-height:150%;mso-bidi-font-family:Arial"> and apparently in satisfactoryncondition, except Echosounder was found not fitted, </span><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size:10.0pt;line-height:150%;mso-ansi-language:EN-GB">BPI was foundnnot supplied on board and Charts was found not updated as per last BPI.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height:150%"><b><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size:10.0pt;line-height:150%;mso-ansi-language:EN-GB">&nbsp;&nbsp; <u>Competent of Officers<o:p></o:p></u></span></b></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-indent:7.1pt;line-height:150%"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size:10.0pt;line-height:150%;mso-bidi-font-family:Arial;mso-ansi-language:nEN-GB">The Officer and crew appeared to be competent; all certificates compliednas per STCW standard.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-indent:7.1pt;line-height:150%"><b><u><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size:10.0pt;line-height:150%;mso-bidi-font-family:Arial;nmso-ansi-language:EN-GB">Interassociation of Officers and Crew<o:p></o:p></span></u></b></p><p>nnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnn</p><p class="MsoNormal"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size:10.0pt;mso-bidi-font-family:nArial;mso-ansi-language:EN-GB">&nbsp;&nbsp; Allncrew have good cooperation during the survey.</span><span lang="EN-US"><o:p></o:p></span></p>', '<p class="MsoHeader" style="text-align:justify;line-height:150%"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:9.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:" tahoma",sans-serif"="">ThenWreck Removal &amp; Oil Pollution </span><span lang="IN" style="font-size:9.0pt;nline-height:150%;font-family:" tahoma",sans-serif;mso-ansi-language:in"="">survey</span><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:9.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:" tahoma",sans-serif"="">nof MV. âIntiâ was conducted on 25 November 2025, whilst she berthed at Kalimasnport, Surabaya, Indonesia waiting for cargo loading operation. During thensurvey, we accompanied/ assisted by the Chief Officer, Chief Engineer and crew.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height:150%"><b><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:9.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:" tahoma",sans-serif"="">HULL<o:p></o:p></span></b></p><p class="MsoListParagraph" style="margin-left:0cm;mso-add-space:auto;text-align:njustify;line-height:150%"><span style="font-size:9.0pt;line-height:150%;nfont-family:" tahoma",sans-serif"="">MV. Inti is a 37 years old vessel, t</span><span lang="IN" style="font-size:9.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:" tahoma",sans-serif;="" mso-ansi-language:in"="">he </span><span style="font-size:9.0pt;line-height:150%;nfont-family:" tahoma",sans-serif"="">vessel</span><span lang="IN" style="font-size:n9.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:" tahoma",sans-serif;mso-ansi-language:in"="">nwas</span><span lang="IN" style="font-size:9.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:n" tahoma",sans-serif;mso-ansi-language:en-gb"=""> </span><span lang="IN" style="font-size:9.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:" tahoma",sans-serif;="" mso-ansi-language:in"="">a</span><span style="font-size:9.0pt;line-height:150%;nfont-family:" tahoma",sans-serif"=""> single hull </span><span lang="IN" style="font-size:9.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:" tahoma",sans-serif;="" mso-ansi-language:in"="">steel</span><span style="font-size:9.0pt;line-height:n150%;font-family:" tahoma",sans-serif"=""> General Cargo with dimension </span><span style="font-size:9.0pt;line-height:150%">LPP = 49.65 m, B</span><span style="font-size:9.0pt;line-height:150%;mso-ansi-language:IN"> </span><span style="font-size:9.0pt;line-height:150%">= 11.00 m</span><span style="font-size:9.0pt;line-height:150%;mso-ansi-language:IN"> </span><span style="font-size:9.0pt;line-height:150%">H = 5.80 m</span><span style="font-size:9.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:" tahoma",sans-serif"="">, GT 805nand NT 297.<span style="color:red"> </span>The Vessel was registered at Surabayanand under Classification of Biro Klasifikasi Indonesia (BKI). The vessel </span><span lang="IN" style="font-size:9.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:" tahoma",sans-serif;="" mso-ansi-language:in"="">was </span><span style="font-size:9.0pt;line-height:150%;nfont-family:" tahoma",sans-serif"="">built by Kabushiki K.K. Zosenso, Japan<span style="color:red"> </span>in 1988. Reported, the vessel has a valid ClassnCertificate i.e: Hull</span><span lang="IN" style="font-size:9.0pt;line-height:n150%;font-family:" tahoma",sans-serif;mso-ansi-language:in"=""> Class</span><span style="font-size:9.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:" tahoma",sans-serif"="">nCertificate, Tonnage Certificate and Load Line Certificate as well as anStatutory Certificate.<span style="color:red"> </span></span><span lang="IN" style="font-size:9.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:" tahoma",sans-serif;="" mso-ansi-language:in"="">The visible shell plating was found well coated withnslightly rusty and deformed/ dent at several places but free from doublers. Bulwarksnsurrounded main deck was found partly corroded/ holed.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify;line-height:150%"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:9.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:" tahoma",sans-serif"="">Duringnthe survey, we found that Main deck was found rusty. Anchor &amp; Mooring Winchesnwere found in satisfactory condition but not fitted with save-alls. &nbsp;Bollards, rollers, fairleads were found rusty/ncorroded. The superstructure and accommodation space were found satisfactory. Weathertightndoors were found corroded at lower part and without Open/ Close marking.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height:150%"><b><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:9.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:" tahoma",sans-serif"="">CARGOnHOLDS / COMPARTMENTS<o:p></o:p></span></b></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify;line-height:150%"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:9.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:" tahoma",sans-serif"="">ThenVessel was fitted with 1 (one) Cargo Hold and 1 (one) unit Crawler Crane at Forwardnof cargo hold. The internal structure and tank top were found in satisfactoryncondition. The Hatch covers were found rusty. The cargo hold bilge was foundnwater and messy. Suction test of Bilge wells and tightness test of Hatch coversnhave not been tested due to no power supply.&nbsp;</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify;line-height:150%"><b><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:9.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:" tahoma",sans-serif"="">NON-CARGOnTANKS:<o:p></o:p></span></b></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify;line-height:150%"><span lang="IN" style="font-size:9.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:" tahoma",sans-serif;="" mso-ansi-language:in"="">The </span><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:9.0pt;nline-height:150%;font-family:" tahoma",sans-serif"="">V</span><span lang="IN" style="font-size:9.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:" tahoma",sans-serif;="" mso-ansi-language:in"="">essel </span><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:9.0pt;nline-height:150%;font-family:" tahoma",sans-serif"="">fitted with 6 WBT ( 1 â 3 (Pn&amp; S)), Fore peak and After peak Tanks. The internal structure of WBT was partlynrusty. Overflow test was carried out by the crew on next day and found innsatisfactory condition.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify;line-height:150%"><b><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:9.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:" tahoma",sans-serif"="">MACHINERY<o:p></o:p></span></b></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify;line-height:150%"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:9.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:" tahoma",sans-serif"="">ThenVessel was equipped with 1 (one) unit of Niigata Type 6 M 28 BGT with 1,000 HPnx 350 Rpm and equipped with 1 (one) unit Auxiliary Engine of Yanmar Type 6 HAL-Mn@136 HP (in Engine room) and Shaft Generator with no data,<span style="color:red"> </span>and 1 unit Emergency Generator (no data) in Boatndeck.<span style="color:red"> </span>The Engine Room was located in the aftnarea. Main Engine, Auxiliary Engines reported in working order. &nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify;line-height:150%"><b><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:9.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:" tahoma",sans-serif"="">POLLUTION<o:p></o:p></span></b></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify;line-height:150%"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:9.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:" tahoma",sans-serif"="">SOPEPnwas found not complete, Scupper plugs and Oil Absorbent were found not availablenon board. FO Air vents, and winches were found not fitted with save-alls.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify;line-height:150%"><b><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:9.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:" tahoma",sans-serif"="">NAVIGATION<o:p></o:p></span></b></p><p>nnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnn</p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify;line-height:150%"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size:9.0pt;line-height:150%;font-family:" tahoma",sans-serif"="">Navigationnand communication fitted on the Bridge such Magnetic Compass, Radar, AIS, GPS,nVHF Radios etc., but Echo Sounder not fitted. Navigational Charts werensufficient for trading area and but not corrected as per last BPI and BPI wasnfound not supplied on board regularly.&nbsp; Changeoverninstruction for emergency steering was found not posted.<o:p></o:p></span></p>', '<p>The vessel was found in satisfactory structural condition but several items to be repaired/rectified.&nbsp; Bridge equipment, Crew and Ship Management are still can be improved. Pollution prevention and equipment to be completed/ rectified.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>', '2025-10-18', '2026-10-18', NOW(), NOW()) ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET status = EXCLUDED.status, summary = EXCLUDED.summary;
INSERT INTO surveys (id, vessel_id, surveyor_id, broker_id, surveyor_name, condition_type, status, form_status, location, date_of_survey, due_date, concern_from_surveyor, resume_from_surveyor, summary, policy_period_start, policy_period_end, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (543, 421, 3, 9, NULL, 'Survey', 'Outstanding', 'draft', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2025-10-16', '2026-10-16', NOW(), NOW()) ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET status = EXCLUDED.status, summary = EXCLUDED.summary;
