m</span><span tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="font-size: 9pt; line-height: 18px;"><span style="font-size: 14px;">, GT 1089 and NT 415.</span><span style="color: red; font-size: 14px;">&nbsp;</span><span style="font-size: 14px;">The Vessel was registered at Surabaya and under Classification of Biro Klasifikasi Indonesia (BKI). The vessel&nbsp;</span></span><span lang="IN" tahoma",sans-serif;="" mso-ansi-language:in"="" style="line-height: 18px;">was&nbsp;</span><span tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="font-size: 9pt; line-height: 18px;"><span style="font-size: 14px;">built by Mategata Zosen Co,.Ltd., Japan</span><span style="color: red; font-size: 14px;">&nbsp;</span><span style="font-size: 14px;">in 1989.&nbsp;Reported, the vessel has a valid Class Certificate i.e: Hull</span></span><span lang="IN" tahoma",sans-serif;mso-ansi-language:in"="" style="line-height: 18px;">&nbsp;Class</span><span tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="font-size: 9pt; line-height: 18px;"><span style="font-size: 14px;">&nbsp;Certificate, Tonnage Certificate and Load Line Certificate as well as a Statutory Certificate.</span><span style="color: red; font-size: 14px;">&nbsp;</span></span><span lang="IN" tahoma",sans-serif;="" mso-ansi-language:in"="" style="line-height: 18px;">The visible shell plating was found in satisfactory condition. But&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">Draft and Plimsoll / Load line marks were found faded.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="line-height: 18px;">During the survey, we found that the Superstructure and accommodation space were found satisfactory.&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">Main deck was found rusty.&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">Railing at forward area was found partly missing and dented.&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">Fore deck was found messy.&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">Hatch coaming at forward area was found corroded.&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">Bulwark at forward area was found corroded.&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">Roller at forward area was found corroded and partly missing and&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">Forward compartment at below fore deck was found corroded</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: 21px;"><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="font-size: 9pt; line-height: 18px;"><span style="font-size: 14px;">CARGO HOLDS / COMPARTMENTS</span><o:p></o:p></span></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="line-height: 18px;">The Vessel was fitted with 1 (one) Cargo Hold and 1 (one) unit Crawler Crane at Middle of cargo hold.&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">Internal structure of cargo hold was found in satisfactory condition, but t</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">ank top was found doubler at fore area.<span style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);">&nbsp;</span></span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);">Bilge wells and Suction test of bilge well were found in satisfactory condition.&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">Hatch covers panel and rubber sealing has not been inspected due to operational reasons and&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">Hose test to Hatch covers has been carried out and were found no leakages to the cargo hold.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="font-size: 9pt; line-height: 18px;"><span style="font-size: 14px;">NON-CARGO TANKS:</span><o:p></o:p></span></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span lang="IN" tahoma",sans-serif;="" mso-ansi-language:in"="" style="line-height: 18px;">The&nbsp;</span><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="line-height: 18px;">V</span><span lang="IN" tahoma",sans-serif;="" mso-ansi-language:in"="" style="line-height: 18px;">essel&nbsp;</span><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="line-height: 18px;">fitted with 6 WBT (1 â 3 (P &amp; S)), Fore peak and After peak Tanks.&nbsp;<span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); text-align: left;">Internal structure of WBT</span></span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">&nbsp;had not been inspected due to operational reasons and&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">Ballast tanks pressure test has been carried out and was found no leakages to the cargo hold.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="font-size: 9pt; line-height: 18px;"><span style="font-size: 14px;">MACHINERY</span><o:p></o:p></span></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="line-height: 18px;">The Vessel was equipped with 1 (one) unit of Engine Diesel Akasaka Type K 28 R with 1,000 HP x 340 Rpm and equipped with 2 (two) units Auxiliary Engine i.e. Deutz Type F 4 912 with 54 HP and Deutz Type BF 6L 913 C with 135 HP (in Engine room) and&nbsp;</span><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="font-size: 9pt; line-height: 18px;"><span style="font-size: 14px;">2 (two) units Emergency Generator (no data) in Boat deck.</span><span style="color: red; font-size: 14px;">&nbsp;</span><span style="font-size: 14px;">The Engine Room was located in the aft area. Main Engine, Auxiliary Engines reported in working order. &nbsp;&nbsp;</span></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="font-size: 9pt; line-height: 18px;"><span style="font-size: 14px;">POLLUTION</span><o:p></o:p></span></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); text-align: left;">Bunker Manifolds and Fuel air vents was found in satisfactory condition, but SOPEP Locker was found not available.&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">FO and LO air vents on P &amp; S Main deck / Gangway were found not fitted with save-alls / drip tray.&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">Scupper plugs were found not available and&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">Oil absorbents were found not available.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="font-size: 9pt; line-height: 18px;"><span style="font-size: 14px;">NAVIGATION</span><o:p></o:p></span></span></p><p></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="line-height: 18px;">Navigation and communication fitted on the Bridge such Gyro Compass, Magnetic Compass, Radar, AIS, Echo Sounder, GPS, VHF Radios etc. Navigational Charts were sufficient for trading area but not updated as per last BPI and NTM / BPI was found not supplied on board regularly.&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">Changeover instructions from emergency steering were found not posted / displayed.</span></p>', '<p>The vessel was found in satisfactory structural condition but several items to be repaired/rectified.&nbsp; Bridge equipment was found satisfactory but NTM/ BPI to be supplied, Charts to be updated, and C<span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); text-indent: -11.6px; font-size: 0.875rem;">hangeover instructions from emergency steering to be posted/ displayed</span><span style="font-size: 0.875rem;">. The Crew and Ship Management are still can be improved. Pollution prevention and equipment was found satisfactory but SOPEP, Scupper plugs, Oil absorbents to be provided and&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">FO and LO air vents on P &amp; S Main deck / Gangway to be fitted</span></p>', '2025-12-24', '2026-12-24', NOW(), NOW()) ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET status = EXCLUDED.status, summary = EXCLUDED.summary;
INSERT INTO surveys (id, vessel_id, surveyor_id, broker_id, surveyor_name, condition_type, status, form_status, location, date_of_survey, due_date, concern_from_surveyor, resume_from_surveyor, summary, policy_period_start, policy_period_end, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (614, 327, 3, 9, NULL, 'Survey', 'Outstanding', 'draft', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-01-29', '2027-01-29', NOW(), NOW()) ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET status = EXCLUDED.status, summary = EXCLUDED.summary;
INSERT INTO surveys (id, vessel_id, surveyor_id, broker_id, surveyor_name, condition_type, status, form_status, location, date_of_survey, due_date, concern_from_surveyor, resume_from_surveyor, summary, policy_period_start, policy_period_end, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (615, 326, 3, NULL, NULL, 'Survey', 'Outstanding', 'draft', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-01-29', '2027-01-29', NOW(), NOW()) ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET status = EXCLUDED.status, summary = EXCLUDED.summary;
INSERT INTO surveys (id, vessel_id, surveyor_id, broker_id, surveyor_name, condition_type, status, form_status, location, date_of_survey, due_date, concern_from_surveyor, resume_from_surveyor, summary, policy_period_start, policy_period_end, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (616, 464, 3, 9, NULL, 'Survey', 'Outstanding', 'draft', NULL, NULL, '2026-03-09', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-02-07', '2027-02-07', NOW(), NOW()) ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET status = EXCLUDED.status, summary = EXCLUDED.summary;
INSERT INTO surveys (id, vessel_id, surveyor_id, broker_id, surveyor_name, condition_type, status, form_status, location, date_of_survey, due_date, concern_from_surveyor, resume_from_surveyor, summary, policy_period_start, policy_period_end, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (617, 463, 8, 9, 'Twin Suganda Syahputra Aruan', 'Survey', 'Completed', 'complete', 'Merak', '2026-01-25', '2026-02-20', '<p><u style="font-weight: bolder; font-size: 0.875rem;"><span lang="EN-GB" style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);">Structural compliance with general marine industry standards</span></u></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);">-Â FO and LO air vents on P & S Main deck were found not fitted with save-alls/ drip tray<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);">-Â Scupper plugs were found not available<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);">-Â Oil absorbents were found not available</span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);">Â -Â </span><span style="font-size: 0.875rem;">Some of fairlead were found wastage</span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><u><span lang="EN-GB">Bridge Management.</span></u></span><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span lang="EN-GB">Implemented by shipâs crew but still can be improved.</span><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><u><span lang="EN-GB">Navigational equipment</span></u></span><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span lang="IN">TheÂ </span><span lang="EN-US">navigation and communication wereÂ </span><span lang="IN">foundÂ </span><span lang="EN-US">fitted</span><span lang="IN">Â on board</span><span lang="EN-US">Â and apparently in satisfactory condition, but NTM/ BPI was found not supplied on boardÂ </span>andÂ Changeover instructions from emergency steering were found not posted / displayed.</span></p>', '<p class="MsoNormal"><span lang="EN-US">The WreckrnRemoval & Oil PollutionÂ </span><span lang="IN">survey</span><span lang="EN-US">Â of MV.rnâPutri Mulya IIIâ was conducted on 25 January 2026, whilst she anchored at Merak anchorage, Banten, Indonesia waiting for cargo loading operation. During thernsurvey, we accompanied/ assisted by the Chief Officer, Chief Engineer andrncrew.</span><o:p></o:p></p>', '<p class="MsoNormal"><b><span lang="EN-US">HULL</span></b><o:p></o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal">MV. Putri Mulya III is 42 years old vessel, t<span lang="IN">heÂ </span>vessel<span lang="IN">Â wasÂ a</span>Â single hullÂ <span lang="IN">steel</span>Â welded construction withrndimension LOA = 68.84 m, BÂ = 11.50 mÂ Hrn= 7.20 m, GT 1418 and NT 754.Â The Vessel was registered at Pontianak and under Classification of Biro Klasifikasi Indonesia (BKI). The vesselÂ <span lang="IN">wasÂ </span>built by Yoshida Dockyard Co,.Ltd., JapanÂ in 1984.Â Reported, the vessel has a valid ClassrnCertificate i.e: Hull<span lang="IN">Â Class</span>Â Certificate,rnTonnage Certificate and Load Line Certificate as well as a StatutoryrnCertificate.Â <span lang="IN">The visible shellrnplating was found in satisfactory condition. TheÂ </span>Draft and Plimsollrn/ Load line marks were found legible.Â <o:p></o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span lang="EN-US" style="">During thernsurvey, we found that the Superstructure and accommodation space were foundrnsatisfactory. The m</span>ain deck, hatch coaming, fore bulwark, handrails were found maintained and painted condition. However, some of fairlead was found wastage and all bollards were found not mark with SWL.Â Â </span><span style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 0);"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"><b style=""><span lang="EN-US" style="">CARGOrnHOLDS / COMPARTMENTS</span></b><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span lang="EN-US" style="">The Vesselrnwas fitted with 1 (one) Cargo Hold and 1 (one) unit Crawler Crane at Middle ofrncargo hold.Â </span>Internal structure of cargo hold was found inrnsatisfactory condition,Â  tank top was found in satisfactory condition, Bilgernwells and Suction test of bilge well were found in satisfactoryrncondition.Â Hatch covers panel and rubber sealing were found in satisfactory condition. The ballast pressure test and Hose test to hatch cover has not been carry out yet due to bad weather and safety reason.Â Â </span><span style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 0);"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"><b style=""><span lang="EN-US" style="">NON-CARGOrnTANKS:</span></b><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span lang="IN" style="">TheÂ </span><span lang="EN-US" style="">V</span><span lang="IN" style="">esselÂ </span><span lang="EN-US" style="">fitted with 6 WBT (1 â 3 (P & S)), Forernpeak and After peak Tanks.Â Internal structure of WBT</span>Â has been inspected and found the plating were in fair condition, no wastage and no significant corrosion.Â Â </span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"><b style=""><span lang="EN-US" style="">MACHINERY</span></b><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span lang="EN-US">The Vesselrnwas equipped with 1 (one) unit of </span><span lang="EN-US">Â DieselÂ engineÂ </span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">with maker Akasa DM28 AFD powered 1200 HP at 390 RPM was found in satisfactory conditionÂ </span><span style="font-size: 0.875rem;">and equipped with 3 (three) units Auxiliary Engine i.e. AE1 : YanmarÂ  with 700 HP, AE II : Mitsubishi Type 4D34 with 85 HP and AE III : YanmarÂ  30 kVA (in Engine room)rnand 1 (one) unit Emergency Generator (no data) in Boat deck.Â ThernEngine Room was located in the aft area. Main Engine, Auxiliary Enginesrnreported in working order. The Bilge high level alarm was found in working order.Â </span></span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"><b style=""><span lang="EN-US" style="">POLLUTION</span></b><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);">Bunker Manifolds and Fuel air vents was found inrnsatisfactory condition, but FO andrnLO air vents on P & S Main deck were found not fitted with drip tray.Â Scupper plugs were not available, andÂ Oilrnabsorbents were found not available.</span><span style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 0);"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"><b style=""><span lang="EN-US" style="">NAVIGATION</span></b><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span lang="EN-US" style="">Navigationrnand communication fitted on the Bridge such Gyro Compass, Magnetic Compass,rnRadar, AIS, Echo Sounder, GPS, VHF Radios etc. Navigational Charts werernsufficient for trading area but not updated as per last BPI and NTM / BPI wasrnfound not supplied on board regularly.Â </span>Changeover instructions fromrnemergency steering were found not posted / displayed.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><span lang="EN-GB" style=""><u style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);">COMPOTENT OFFICER</u></span></span><span style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span lang="EN-GB">The Officer and crew appeared to be competent; all certificates complied as per STCW standard.</span><o:p></o:p></span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><u><span lang="EN-GB">INTERASSOCIATION OF OFFICERS AND CREW</span></u></span><o:p></o:p></span></p><p></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span lang="EN-GB" style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);">Â All crew have good cooperation during the survey.</span></p>', '2026-01-21', '2027-01-21', NOW(), NOW()) ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET status = EXCLUDED.status, summary = EXCLUDED.summary;
INSERT INTO surveys (id, vessel_id, surveyor_id, broker_id, surveyor_name, condition_type, status, form_status, location, date_of_survey, due_date, concern_from_surveyor, resume_from_surveyor, summary, policy_period_start, policy_period_end, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (618, 341, NULL, 8, NULL, 'Survey', 'Outstanding', 'draft', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-01-01', '2027-01-01', NOW(), NOW()) ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET status = EXCLUDED.status, summary = EXCLUDED.summary;
INSERT INTO surveys (id, vessel_id, surveyor_id, broker_id, surveyor_name, condition_type, status, form_status, location, date_of_survey, due_date, concern_from_surveyor, resume_from_surveyor, summary, policy_period_start, policy_period_end, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (619, 233, NULL, 8, NULL, 'Survey', 'Outstanding', 'draft', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-01-01', '2027-01-01', NOW(), NOW()) ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET status = EXCLUDED.status, summary = EXCLUDED.summary;
INSERT INTO surveys (id, vessel_id, surveyor_id, broker_id, surveyor_name, condition_type, status, form_status, location, date_of_survey, due_date, concern_from_surveyor, resume_from_surveyor, summary, policy_period_start, policy_period_end, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (620, 465, 3, 9, NULL, 'Survey', 'Outstanding', 'draft', NULL, NULL, '2026-02-02', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-01-03', '2027-01-03', NOW(), NOW()) ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET status = EXCLUDED.status, summary = EXCLUDED.summary;
INSERT INTO surveys (id, vessel_id, surveyor_id, broker_id, surveyor_name, condition_type, status, form_status, location, date_of_survey, due_date, concern_from_surveyor, resume_from_surveyor, summary, policy_period_start, policy_period_end, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (621, 466, 8, 9, 'FAJAR TRIHASTYANTO KUNCORO', 'Survey', 'Outstanding', 'draft', 'GRESIK ANCHORAGE, GRESIK - INDONESIA', '2026-01-24', '2026-03-02', '<p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 26.9pt; text-indent: -17.85pt; line-height: 21px;"><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><u><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 20px;">Structural compliance with general marine industry standards</span></u></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 26.9pt; text-indent: -17.85pt; line-height: 21px;"><span style="font-size: 13.3333px;">- H</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">ead and pipe of Fuel air vents were found damage/ malfunction/ rusty and corroded</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 26.9pt; text-indent: -17.85pt; line-height: 21px;"><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">-Â </span><span style="font-size: 0.875rem; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);">Save-alls were found not fitted on Emergency generator,Â </span><span style="font-size: 0.875rem; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);">Hydraulic operating handle of Anchor & Mooring Windlass andÂ </span><span style="font-size: 0.875rem; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);">Aft Mooring Winches</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 26.9pt; text-indent: -17.85pt; line-height: 21px;"><span style="font-size: 0.875rem; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);">- Oil absorbents were found not available</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 26.9pt; text-indent: -17.85pt; line-height: 21px;"><span style="font-size: 0.875rem; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);">-Â </span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">Draft marks, Plimsoll/ Load line marks, and stern ship''s name were found faded</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 26.9pt; text-indent: -17.85pt; line-height: 21px;"><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">-Â </span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">Main deck was found rusty</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 26.9pt; text-indent: -17.85pt; line-height: 21px;"><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">-Â </span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-indent: -17.85pt;">Bulwark was found heavy corroded</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 26.9pt; text-indent: -17.85pt; line-height: 21px;"><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-indent: -17.85pt;">-Â </span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">Railings were found partly missing and broken/ corroded</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 26.9pt; text-indent: -17.85pt; line-height: 21px;"><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">-Â </span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">Stanchion, Top plate and Longitudinal Stiffener of Hatch coamings were found heavy corroded</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 26.9pt; text-indent: -17.85pt; line-height: 21px;"><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">-Â </span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">Hydraulic operating handles of Hatch cover were found leakages</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 26.9pt; text-indent: -17.85pt; line-height: 21px;"><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">-Â </span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">Vertical ladders on external Hatch coaming were found heavy corroded</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 26.9pt; text-indent: -17.85pt; line-height: 21px;"><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">-Â </span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">Hydrant pipe on Main deck was found leakage</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 26.9pt; text-indent: -17.85pt; line-height: 21px;"><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">-Â </span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">All inclined ladders on outside accommodation were found corroded</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 26.9pt; text-indent: -17.85pt; line-height: 21px;"><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">-Â </span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">Many doublers were found at forward deck</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 26.9pt; text-indent: -17.85pt; line-height: 21px;"><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">-Â </span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">Chain stopper of Anchor and Mooring Windlass (S) was found missing</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 26.9pt; text-indent: -17.85pt; line-height: 21px;"><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">-Â </span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">Hydraulic pipe of Anchor and Mooring Windlass was found tightened with rubber ban</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 26.9pt; text-indent: -17.85pt; line-height: 21px;"><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">-Â </span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">Drums of Aft Mooring Winches were found partly corroded</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 26.9pt; text-indent: -17.85pt; line-height: 21px;"><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">-Â </span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">Watertight doors access to accommodation and cargo hold were found corroded & without Open/ Close marking</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 26.9pt; text-indent: -17.85pt; line-height: 21px;"><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">-Â </span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">Interior of Cargo hold was found rusty and tank top not clean (found cargo residue)</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 26.9pt; text-indent: -17.85pt; line-height: 21px;"><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">- R</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">ubber sealing of Hatch covers was found hardened and partly broken</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 26.9pt; text-indent: -17.85pt; line-height: 21px;"><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">-Â </span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">Ballast tank pressure test has not been carried out due to operational reasons</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 26.9pt; text-indent: -17.85pt; line-height: 21px;"><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><u><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 20px;">Bridge Management.<o:p></o:p></span></u></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 26.9pt; text-indent: -17.85pt; line-height: 21px;"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 20px;">Implemented by shipâs crew but still can be improved.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 26.9pt; text-indent: -17.85pt; line-height: 21px;"><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><u><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 20px;">Navigational equipment</span></u></span><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><u><span lang="IN" style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 20px;"><o:p></o:p></span></u></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 8.7pt; text-indent: -8.7pt; line-height: 21px;"><span lang="IN" style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 20px;">Â Â  TheÂ </span><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 20px;">navigation and communication wereÂ </span><span lang="IN" style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 20px;">foundÂ </span><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 20px;">fitted</span><span lang="IN" style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 20px;">Â on board</span><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 20px;">Â and apparently in satisfactory condition. But Display of Radar and Echo sounder were found not clear, NTM/ BPI was found not supplied on board and Charts were found not updated as per latestÂ </span><span style="font-size: 13.3333px; text-indent: -11.6px;">NTM/ BPI.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: 21px;"><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 20px;">Â Â Â <u>Competent of Officers<o:p></o:p></u></span></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-indent: 7.1pt; line-height: 21px;"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 20px;">The Officer and crew appeared to be competent; all certificates complied as per STCW standard.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-indent: 7.1pt; line-height: 21px;"><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><u><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 20px;">Interassociation of Officers and Crew<o:p></o:p></span></u></span></p><p></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size: 10pt;">Â Â  All crew have good cooperation during the survey.</span></p>', '<p class="MsoHeader" style="text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="line-height: 18px;">The Wreck Removal &amp; Oil Pollution&nbsp;</span><span lang="IN" tahoma",sans-serif;mso-ansi-language:in"="" style="line-height: 18px;">survey</span><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="line-height: 18px;">&nbsp;of MV. âKaltim Express 22â was conducted on 24 January 2026, whilst she was anchored at Gresik anchorage, Gresik, Indonesia waiting for cargo loading operation. During the survey, we were accompanied/ assisted by the Chief Officer, Chief Engineer and crew.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: 21px;"><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="font-size: 9pt; line-height: 18px;"><span style="font-size: 14px;">HULL</span><o:p></o:p></span></span></p><p class="MsoListParagraph" style="margin-left: 0cm; text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="line-height: 18px;">MV. Kaltim Express 22 is 37 years old vessel,&nbsp;</span><span tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="line-height: 18px;">single hull&nbsp;</span><span lang="IN" tahoma",sans-serif;="" mso-ansi-language:in"="" style="line-height: 18px;">steel</span><span tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="line-height: 18px;">&nbsp;General Cargo with dimension LOA = 70.40 M,&nbsp;</span><span style="line-height: 18px;">LPP = 67.65 m, B</span><span style="line-height: 18px;">&nbsp;</span><span style="line-height: 18px;">= 12.50 m</span><span style="line-height: 18px;">&nbsp;</span><span style="line-height: 18px;">H = 6.50 m</span><span tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="font-size: 9pt; line-height: 18px;"><span style="font-size: 14px;">, GT 1,550 and NT 465.</span><span style="color: red; font-size: 14px;">&nbsp;</span><span style="font-size: 14px;">The Vessel was registered at Surabaya and under Classification of Biro Klasifikasi Indonesia (BKI). The vessel&nbsp;</span></span><span lang="IN" tahoma",sans-serif;="" mso-ansi-language:in"="" style="line-height: 18px;">was&nbsp;</span><span tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="font-size: 9pt; line-height: 18px;"><span style="font-size: 14px;">built by Mitsubishi Heavy Industries LTD., Japan</span><span style="color: red; font-size: 14px;">&nbsp;</span><span style="font-size: 14px;">in 1989.&nbsp;Reported, the vessel has a valid Class Certificate i.e: Hull</span></span><span lang="IN" tahoma",sans-serif;mso-ansi-language:in"="" style="line-height: 18px;">&nbsp;&amp; Machinery Class</span><span tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="font-size: 9pt; line-height: 18px;"><span style="font-size: 14px;">&nbsp;Certificate, Tonnage Certificate and Load Line Certificate as well as Statutory Certificates.</span><span style="color: red; font-size: 14px;">&nbsp;</span></span><span lang="IN" tahoma",sans-serif;="" mso-ansi-language:in"="" style="line-height: 18px;">The visible shell plating was found in satisfactory condition. but&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">Draft marks, Plimsoll/ Load line marks, and stern ship''s name were found faded.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: left; line-height: 21px;"><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="line-height: 18px;">During the survey, we found that the Superstructure and accommodation space in satisfactory condition. <font color="#212529">but&nbsp;</font></span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">Main deck was found rusty,&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">Bulwark was found heavy corroded.&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">Railings were found partly missing and broken/ corroded.&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">Stanchion, Top plate and Longitudinal Stiffener of Hatch coamings were found heavy corroded.&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">Hydraulic operating handles of Hatch cover were found leakages.&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">Vertical ladders on external Hatch coaming were found heavy corroded.&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">Hydrant pipe on Main deck was found leakages.&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">All inclined ladders on outside accommodation were found corroded.&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">Many doublers were found at forward deck.&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">Chain stopper of Anchor and Mooring Windlass (S) was found missing.&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">Hydraulic pipe of Anchor and Mooring Windlass was found tightened with rubber ban.&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">Drums of Aft Mooring Winches were found partly corroded.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: 21px;"><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="font-size: 9pt; line-height: 18px;"><span style="font-size: 14px;">CARGO HOLDS / COMPARTMENTS</span><o:p></o:p></span></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="line-height: 18px;">The Vessel was fitted with 1 (one) Cargo Hold and 1 (one) unit Crawler crane at Middle of cargo hold.&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">Internal structure of cargo hold was found</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">&nbsp;rusty and tank top not clean (found cargo residue). Cargo hold bilge was found in fair condition. Suction test has been carried out and found in satisfactory condition.&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">Hatch covers were found in fair condition, but rubber sealing found hardened and partly broken.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="font-size: 9pt; line-height: 18px;"><span style="font-size: 14px;">NON-CARGO TANKS:</span><o:p></o:p></span></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span lang="IN" tahoma",sans-serif;="" mso-ansi-language:in"="" style="line-height: 18px;">The&nbsp;</span><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="line-height: 18px;">V</span><span lang="IN" tahoma",sans-serif;="" mso-ansi-language:in"="" style="line-height: 18px;">essel&nbsp;</span><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="line-height: 18px;">fitted with 4 WBT (1 â 2 (P &amp; S)), Fore peak and After peak Tanks.&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">The&nbsp;</span><span style="font-size: 0.875rem; color: rgb(33, 37, 41); text-align: left;">Internal structure of WBT was found in fair condition.</span><span style="font-size: 0.875rem; color: rgb(33, 37, 41); text-align: left;">&nbsp;</span><span style="font-size: 0.875rem; color: rgb(33, 37, 41); text-align: left;">Ballast tanks pressure test has not been carried out due to operational reasons.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="font-size: 9pt; line-height: 18px;"><span style="font-size: 14px;">MACHINERY</span><o:p></o:p></span></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="line-height: 18px;">The Vessel was equipped with 1 (one) unit of Akasaka Type K 28 FD with 1,400 HP x 400 Rpm and equipped with 2 (two) units Auxiliary Engine Mitsubishi Type 6 D14 - MPT with 2 x 120 HP (in Engine room) and&nbsp;</span><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="font-size: 9pt; line-height: 18px;"><span style="font-size: 14px;">2 (two) units Emergency Generator (no data) on Boat deck.</span><span style="color: red; font-size: 14px;">&nbsp;</span><span style="font-size: 14px;">The Engine Room was located in the aft area.</span></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="font-size: 9pt; line-height: 18px;"><span style="font-size: 14px;">POLLUTION</span><o:p></o:p></span></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); text-align: left;">SOPEP Locker and equipment was found available. Bunker manifolds were found in fair condition. Scupper plugs were found available, but </span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">Head and pipe of Fuel air vents were found damage/ malfunction/ rusty and corroded. Save-alls were found not fitted on Emergency generator,&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">Hydraulic operating handle of Anchor &amp; Mooring Windlass and&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">Aft Mooring Winches. Oil absorbents were found not available.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="font-size: 9pt; line-height: 18px;"><span style="font-size: 14px;">NAVIGATION</span><o:p></o:p></span></span></p><p></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="line-height: 18px;">Navigation and communication fitted on the Bridge such as Gyro Compass, Magnetic Compass, Radar, AIS, Echo Sounder, GPS, VHF Radios etc.&nbsp;</span><span style="font-size: 0.875rem;">Changeover instructions for emergency steering were found posted/ displayed on the bridge.&nbsp;</span><span style="font-size: 0.875rem;">But The Display of Radar and Echo sounder were found not clear. Deviation card was found expired. Navigational Charts were sufficient for trading area but not updated as per last NTM/ BPI and NTM / BPI was found not supplied on board regularly.</span></p>', '<p>The vessel was found in satisfactory structural condition but several items to be repaired/rectified.Â  Bridge equipment was found satisfactory but Display of Radar and Echo sounder to be repaired, NTM/ BPI to be supplied and Charts to be updated. The Crew and Ship Management are still can be improved. Pollution prevention and equipment was found satisfactory but Oil absorbents to be provided.Â </p>', '2026-01-31', '2027-12-31', NOW(), NOW()) ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET status = EXCLUDED.status, summary = EXCLUDED.summary;
INSERT INTO surveys (id, vessel_id, surveyor_id, broker_id, surveyor_name, condition_type, status, form_status, location, date_of_survey, due_date, concern_from_surveyor, resume_from_surveyor, summary, policy_period_start, policy_period_end, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (622, 467, 8, 9, 'Twin Suganda Syahputra Aruan', 'Survey', 'Completed', 'complete', 'Lolak, North Sulawesi', '2026-02-25', '2026-02-07', '<p class="MsoNormal"><b><u>Structural compliance with general marine industryrnstandards</u></b><o:p></o:p></p><p style="text-align: justify; margin-bottom: 0cm; text-indent: -18pt; line-height: 150%;"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style="font-family:Symbol;mso-fareast-font-family:Symbol;mso-bidi-font-family:rnSymbol">Â·<span style="font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-language-override: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: " times="" new="" roman";"="">Â  Â  Â  Â -Â </span></span>SOPEP materials was not provided completely foundrnnot available.<o:p></o:p></p><p style="text-align: justify; margin-bottom: 0cm; text-indent: -18pt; line-height: 150%;"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style="font-family:Symbol;mso-fareast-font-family:Symbol;mso-bidi-font-family:rnSymbol">Â·<span style="font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-language-override: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: " times="" new="" roman";"="">Â  Â  Â  Â -Â </span></span><!--[endif]-->FO air vents were found not fitted with closingrnneck / drip tray.<o:p></o:p></p><p style="text-align: justify; margin-bottom: 0cm; text-indent: -18pt; line-height: 150%;"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style="font-family:Symbol;mso-fareast-font-family:Symbol;mso-bidi-font-family:rnSymbol">Â·<span style="font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-language-override: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: " times="" new="" roman";"="">Â  Â  Â  Â -Â Â </span></span><!--[endif]-->Scupper plugs were found not available.<o:p></o:p></p><p style="text-align: justify; margin-bottom: 0cm; text-indent: -18pt; line-height: 150%;"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style="font-family:Symbol;mso-fareast-font-family:Symbol;mso-bidi-font-family:rnSymbol">Â·<span style="font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-language-override: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: " times="" new="" roman";"="">Â  Â  Â  Â -Â </span></span><!--[endif]-->Oil absorbents were found not available.<o:p></o:p></p><p style="text-align: justify; margin-bottom: 0cm; text-indent: -18pt; line-height: 150%;"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style="font-family:Symbol;mso-fareast-font-family:Symbol;mso-bidi-font-family:rnSymbol">Â·<span style="font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-language-override: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: " times="" new="" roman";"="">Â  Â  Â  Â -Â </span></span><!--[endif]-->The deck was found not marked with anti-slip.<o:p></o:p></p><p style="text-align: justify; margin-bottom: 0cm; text-indent: -18pt; line-height: 150%;"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style="font-family:Symbol;mso-fareast-font-family:Symbol;mso-bidi-font-family:rnSymbol">Â·<span style="font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-language-override: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: " times="" new="" roman";"="">Â  Â  Â  Â -Â </span></span><!--[endif]-->Hydraulic pump of emergency steering was not fittedrnwith save-all.<o:p></o:p></p><p style="text-align: justify; margin-bottom: 0cm; text-indent: -18pt; line-height: 150%;"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style="font-family:Symbol;mso-fareast-font-family:Symbol;mso-bidi-font-family:rnSymbol">Â·<span style="font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-language-override: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: " times="" new="" roman";"="">Â  Â  Â  Â -Â </span></span><!--[endif]-->Bollards was found not marked with SWL.<o:p></o:p></p><p style="text-align: justify; margin-bottom: 0cm; text-indent: -18pt; line-height: 150%;"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style="font-family:Symbol;mso-fareast-font-family:Symbol;mso-bidi-font-family:rnSymbol">Â·<span style="font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-language-override: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: " times="" new="" roman";"="">Â  Â  Â  Â -Â </span></span><!--[endif]-->Mooring ropes at forecaster windlass was foundrnin poor condition.<o:p></o:p></p><p style="text-align: justify; margin-bottom: 0cm; text-indent: -18pt; line-height: 150%;"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style="font-family:Symbol;mso-fareast-font-family:Symbol;mso-bidi-font-family:rnSymbol">Â·<span style="font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-language-override: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: " times="" new="" roman";"="">Â  Â  Â  Â -Â </span></span><!--[endif]-->The main access to accommodation was found notrnfitted with watertight doors.<o:p></o:p></p><p style="text-align: justify; margin-bottom: 0cm; text-indent: -18pt; line-height: 150%;"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style="font-family:Symbol;mso-fareast-font-family:Symbol;mso-bidi-font-family:rnSymbol">Â·<span style="font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-language-override: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: " times="" new="" roman";"="">Â  Â  Â  Â -Â </span></span><!--[endif]-->Cargo hold bilges was found filled withrnremaining last cargo which it has been hardens and clumps.<o:p></o:p></p><p style="text-align: justify; margin-bottom: 0cm; text-indent: -18pt; line-height: 150%;"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style="font-family:Symbol;mso-fareast-font-family:Symbol;mso-bidi-font-family:rnSymbol">Â·<span style="font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-language-override: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: " times="" new="" roman";"="">Â  Â  Â  Â -Â </span></span><!--[endif]-->Cargo holds bilge was not fitted with suctionrnpump.<o:p></o:p></p><p style="text-align: justify; margin-bottom: 0cm; text-indent: -18pt; line-height: 150%;"><!--[if !supportLists]--><span style="font-family:Symbol;mso-fareast-font-family:Symbol;mso-bidi-font-family:rnSymbol">Â·<span style="font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-language-override: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: " times="" new="" roman";"="">Â  Â  Â  Â -Â </span></span>The drain channel of cargo holds no.2 at forernport and starboard side was found wastage / significant corrosion and leakage.</p><p style="text-align: justify; margin-bottom: 0cm; text-indent: -18pt; line-height: 150%;"><span style="font-size: 0.875rem; text-indent: -18pt;">Â  Â  Â  - Some cross joint of cargo holds was found significantrncorrosion, wastage and the rubber sealing were poor condition and some was missing.</span></p><p style="text-align: justify; margin-bottom: 0cm; text-indent: -18pt; line-height: 150%;"><span style="font-size: 0.875rem; text-indent: -18pt;"><br></span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><b><u>Bridge Management.<o:p></o:p></u></b></p><p style="text-align: justify; margin-bottom: 0cm; text-indent: -18pt; line-height: 150%;">rnrn</p><p class="MsoNormal">Implemented by shipâs crew but still can be improved.</p><p class="MsoNormal"><b><u>Navigational equipment<o:p></o:p></u></b></p><p class="MsoNormal">rnrn</p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph">Thernnavigation and communication were found fitted on board and apparently inrnsatisfactory condition, but NTM/ BPI was found not supplied on board, Chartsrnwere found not updated as per latest NTM/ BPI, and Changeover instructions fromrnemergency steering were found not posted / displayed.</p><p class="MsoNormal"><b><u>Competent of Officers</u></b></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph">rnrnrnrn</p><p class="MsoNormal">The Officer and crew appeared to be competent; allrncertificates complied as per STCW standard.</p><p class="MsoNormal"><b><u>Interassociation of Officers and Crew<o:p></o:p></u></b></p><p class="MsoNormal"><o:p>rnrn</o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal">Â All crew have good cooperation during the survey.<o:p></o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal"><o:p></o:p></p>', '<p>The Wreck Removal & Oil Pollution survey of MV. âKelapa Duaâ was conducted on 25 February 2026, whilst she anchored at Lolak anchorage, Sout Sulawesi, Indonesia waiting for cargo loading operation. During the survey, we were accompanied/ assisted by the Chief Officer, Chief Engineer and crew.</p><p>HULL</p><p style="text-align: justify; ">MV. Kelapa Dua is 42 years old vessel, the vessel was a single hull steel General Cargo with dimension LOA = 64.76 m, B = 10.50 m H = 6.00 m, GT 1105 and NT 332. The Vessel was registered at Tanjung Perak, Surabaya and under Classification of Biro Klasifikasi Indonesia (BKI). The vessel was built by MIURA ZOSENSO, Japan in 1983. Reported, the vessel has a valid Class Certificate i.e: Hull Class Certificate, Tonnage Certificate and Load Line Certificate as well as a Statutory Certificate. The visible shell plating was found in satisfactory condition. The Draft and Plimsoll / Load line marks and ship''s name were found legible.</p><p style="text-align: justify; ">During the survey, we found that the Superstructure and accommodation space were found satisfactory. The deck was found not marked with anti-slip, ship''s railing throughout the vessel was found in fair and maintained condition. The bollards and roller structural were found in fair condition. However, it was not fitted with SWL. The mooring ropes at fore windlass was found in poor condition. The fuel vents were not marked and not fitted with closing neck or drip trays. No scupper plug provided onboard and the SOPEP materials was not completely supplied onboard.Â </p><p style="text-align: justify; "><br></p><p>CARGO HOLDS / COMPARTMENTS</p><p style="text-align: justify; "><span style="font-size: 0.875rem;">The Vessel was fitted with 2 (two) Cargo Hold and 1 (one) unit Crawler Crane at Middle of cargo hold. Internal structure of cargo hold such as tank top, side frame and fore/aft bulkhead were found in fair condition. The bilge was found filled with remaining last cargo which it has been hardens and clumps, furthermore the bilge was not fitted with suction pump. Hatch coaming was found in fair condition. In generally. the h</span><span style="font-size: 0.875rem;">atch covers panel was found in fair condition. However, some of cross joint were found wastage and significant corrosion, the rubber sealing was found in poor condition and some it was missing. The drain channel of CH1 at fore port and starboard side was found wastage and leakage condition. Based on hose tested, the cargo holds no.1 and no.2 were not watertight condition.Â </span></p><p style="text-align: justify; "><span style="font-size: 0.875rem;"><br></span></p><p>NON-CARGO TANKS:</p><p><span style="font-size: 0.875rem;">The Vessel fitted with 6 WBT (1 â 3 (P & S)), Fore peak and After peak Tanks. Internal structure of WBT no.2 - 3 P&S has been inspected and found generally the internal structures of plates were significant corrosion. The ballast tanks pressure test has been carried out and was found no leakages to the cargo hold and to others BW tanks.</span></p><p><span style="font-size: 0.875rem;"><br></span></p><p>MACHINERY</p><p>The Vessel was equipped with 1 (one) unit of Engine Diesel NigataType 6 M 28 AFTE with 1200 HP x 380 Rpm and equipped with 2 (two) units Auxiliary Engine i.e. Yanmar Type 3 TL with 54 HP and Type 6 CHI-HTN with 120 HP (in Engine room) and 2 (two) units Emergency Generator (no data) in Boat deck. The Engine Room was located in the aft area. Main Engine, Auxiliary Engines reported in working order.Â  Â </p><p><br></p><p>POLLUTION</p><p>Bunker station was found in fair condition and fitted with save-all. However, the fuel air vents were not marked and fitted with closing neck or drip tray. The SOPEP was found not provided with completely materials. Scupper plugs were found not available and Oil absorbents were found not available.</p><p><br></p><p>NAVIGATION</p><p>Navigation and communication fitted on the Bridge such Gyro Compass, Magnetic Compass, Radar, AIS, Echo Sounder, GPS, VHF Radios etc. Navigational Charts were sufficient for trading area but not updated as per last BPI and NTM / BPI was found not supplied on board regularly. Changeover instructions from emergency steering were found not posted / displayed.</p><div bis_skin_checked="1"><br></div>', '<p>The vessel MV. Kelapa Dua was found in fair condition. Some of structural condition as deficiency items need to be repaired/rectified.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>', '2026-01-08', '2027-01-08', NOW(), NOW()) ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET status = EXCLUDED.status, summary = EXCLUDED.summary;
INSERT INTO surveys (id, vessel_id, surveyor_id, broker_id, surveyor_name, condition_type, status, form_status, location, date_of_survey, due_date, concern_from_surveyor, resume_from_surveyor, summary, policy_period_start, policy_period_end, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (623, 468, 8, 9, 'FAJAR TRIHASTYANTO KUNCORO', 'Survey', 'Outstanding', 'complete', 'GRESIK ANCHORAGE, GRESIK - INDONESIA', '2026-01-15', '2026-02-19', '<p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 26.9pt; text-indent: -17.85pt; line-height: 21px;"><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><u><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 20px;">Structural compliance with general marine industry standards</span></u></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 26.9pt; text-indent: -17.85pt; line-height: 21px;"><span style="font-size: 13.3333px;">-&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">SOPEP Equipment was found not completed</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 26.9pt; text-indent: -17.85pt; line-height: 21px;"><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">-&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">Bunker connection was found obstructed with foreign materials</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 26.9pt; text-indent: -17.85pt; line-height: 21px;"><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">-&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">Fuel air vents, Bunker manifolds, Anchor windlass hydraulic operating handle, and Emergency generator (S) were found not fitted with save-alls/ drip tray</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 26.9pt; text-indent: -17.85pt; line-height: 21px;"><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">-&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">Scupper plugs were found not available</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 26.9pt; text-indent: -17.85pt; line-height: 21px;"><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">- Oil absorbent</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">s were found not available</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 26.9pt; text-indent: -17.85pt; line-height: 21px;"><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">-&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">Draft mark at middle port side was found faded</span></p><p style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41);">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;- Bulwark at corner stern starboard side was found dented / crack and bulwark at forward area (P &amp; S) was found corroded</p><p style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41);">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;- Hatch coaming stanchions at forward and aft area were found corroded</p><p style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41);">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;- Access door to cargo hold at forward was found heavy rusty</p><p style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41);">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;- Anchor chains were found heavy rusty</p><p style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41);">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;- Chain stopper foundations were found corroded</p><p style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41);">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;- Starboard side Anchor windlass brake lining was found broken</p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 26.9pt; text-indent: -17.85pt; line-height: 21px;"><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">-&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">Watertight doors were found without Open / Close marking</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 26.9pt; text-indent: -17.85pt; line-height: 21px;"><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><u><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 20px;">Bridge Management.<o:p></o:p></span></u></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 26.9pt; text-indent: -17.85pt; line-height: 21px;"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 20px;">Implemented by shipâs crew but still can be improved.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 26.9pt; text-indent: -17.85pt; line-height: 21px;"><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><u><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 20px;">Navigational equipment</span></u></span><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><u><span lang="IN" style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 20px;"><o:p></o:p></span></u></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 8.7pt; text-indent: -8.7pt; line-height: 21px;"><span lang="IN" style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 20px;">&nbsp;&nbsp; The&nbsp;</span><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 20px;">navigation and communication were&nbsp;</span><span lang="IN" style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 20px;">found&nbsp;</span><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 20px;">fitted</span><span lang="IN" style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 20px;">&nbsp;on board</span><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 20px;">&nbsp;and apparently in satisfactory condition, but NTM/ BPI was found not supplied on board and Charts were found not updated as per latest&nbsp;</span><span style="font-size: 13.3333px; text-indent: -11.6px;">NTM/ BPI.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: 21px;"><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 20px;">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<u>Competent of Officers<o:p></o:p></u></span></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-indent: 7.1pt; line-height: 21px;"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 20px;">The Officer and crew appeared to be competent; all certificates complied as per STCW standard.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-indent: 7.1pt; line-height: 21px;"><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><u><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 20px;">Interassociation of Officers and Crew<o:p></o:p></span></u></span></p><p></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size: 10pt;">&nbsp;&nbsp; All crew have good cooperation during the survey.</span></p>', '<p class="MsoHeader" style="text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 18px;">The Wreck Removal &amp; Oil Pollution&nbsp;</span><span lang="IN" tahoma",sans-serif;mso-ansi-language:in"="" style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 18px;">survey</span><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 18px;">&nbsp;of MV. âSarana Suksesâ was conducted on 15 January 2026, whilst she anchored at Gresik anchorage, Gresik, Indonesia waiting for cargo loading operation. During the survey, we were accompanied/ assisted by the Chief Officer, Chief Engineer and crew.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: 21px;"><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="font-size: 9pt; line-height: 18px;"><span style="font-size: 14px;">HULL</span><o:p></o:p></span></span></p><p class="MsoListParagraph" style="margin-left: 0cm; text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 18px;">MV. Sarana Sukses is 36 years old vessel, t</span><span lang="IN" tahoma",sans-serif;="" mso-ansi-language:in"="" style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 18px;">he&nbsp;</span><span tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 18px;">vessel</span><span lang="IN" tahoma",sans-serif;mso-ansi-language:in"="" style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 18px;">&nbsp;was</span><span lang="IN" tahoma",sans-serif;mso-ansi-language:en-gb"="" style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 18px;">&nbsp;</span><span lang="IN" tahoma",sans-serif;="" mso-ansi-language:in"="" style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 18px;">a</span><span tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 18px;">&nbsp;single hull&nbsp;</span><span lang="IN" tahoma",sans-serif;="" mso-ansi-language:in"="" style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 18px;">steel</span><span tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 18px;">&nbsp;General Cargo with dimension&nbsp;</span><span style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 18px;">LPP = 70.40 m, B</span><span style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 18px;">&nbsp;</span><span style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 18px;">= 12.00 m</span><span style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 18px;">&nbsp;</span><span style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 18px;">H = <span style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);">6.50</span> m</span><span tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="font-size: 9pt; line-height: 18px;"><span style="font-size: 14px;">, GT 1353 and NT 705.</span><span style="color: red; font-size: 14px;">&nbsp;</span><span style="font-size: 14px;">The Vessel was registered at Surabaya and under Classification of Biro Klasifikasi Indonesia (BKI). The vessel&nbsp;</span></span><span lang="IN" tahoma",sans-serif;="" mso-ansi-language:in"="" style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 18px;">was&nbsp;</span><span tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="font-size: 9pt; line-height: 18px;"><span style="font-size: 14px;">built by K.K Murakami Zosenho, Japan</span><span style="color: red; font-size: 14px;">&nbsp;</span><span style="font-size: 14px;">in 1990. <span style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);">Reported, the vessel has a valid Class Certificate i.e: Hull &amp; Machinery</span></span></span><span style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span lang="IN" tahoma",sans-serif;mso-ansi-language:in"="" style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 18px;">&nbsp;Class</span><span tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="font-size: 9pt; line-height: 18px;"><span style="font-size: 14px;">&nbsp;Certificate, Tonnage Certificate and Load Line Certificate as well as a Statutory Certificate.</span><span style="color: red; font-size: 14px;">&nbsp;</span></span><span lang="IN" tahoma",sans-serif;="" mso-ansi-language:in"="" style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 18px;">The visible shell plating was found in satisfactory condition. But&nbsp;</span></span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;"><span style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);">D</span>raft mark at middle port side was found faded.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 18px;">During the survey, we found that the Main deck was found to be in satisfactory condition. The Superstructure and accommodation space were found satisfactory. Watertight doors were found without Open/ Close marking.</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">&nbsp;Bulwark at corner stern starboard side was found dented/ crack and bulwark at forward area (P &amp; S) was found corroded,&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">Hatch coaming stanchions at forward and aft area were found corroded,&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">Access door to cargo hold at forward was found heavy rusty,&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">Anchor chains were found heavy rusty,&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">Chain stopper foundations were found corroded,&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">Starboard side Anchor windlass brake lining was found broken.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: 21px;"><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="font-size: 9pt; line-height: 18px;"><span style="font-size: 14px;">CARGO HOLDS / COMPARTMENTS</span><o:p></o:p></span></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 18px;">The Vessel was fitted with 1 (one) Cargo Hold and 2 (two) units Crawler Crane at Forward and middle of cargo hold.&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">Internal structure of cargo hold has not been inspected due to safety reasons. The&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">Cargo hold bilge and suction test has not been inspected and tested due to safety reasons.&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">Hatch covers and rubber sealing have not been inspected due to safety and operational reasons.&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">Hose test has not been tested due to operational reasons.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="font-size: 9pt; line-height: 18px;"><span style="font-size: 14px;">NON-CARGO TANKS:</span><o:p></o:p></span></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span lang="IN" tahoma",sans-serif;="" mso-ansi-language:in"="" style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 18px;">The&nbsp;</span><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 18px;">V</span><span lang="IN" tahoma",sans-serif;="" mso-ansi-language:in"="" style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 18px;">essel&nbsp;</span></span><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 18px;"><span style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);">fitted with 6 WBT (1 â 3 (P &amp; S)), Fore peak and After peak Tanks</span>.&nbsp;<span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); text-align: left;">Internal structure of WBT has not been inspected due to safety reasons</span>.&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">Ballast tank pressure test has not been carried out due to operational reasons</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="font-size: 9pt; line-height: 18px;"><span style="font-size: 14px;">MACHINERY</span><o:p></o:p></span></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 18px;">The Vessel was equipped with 1 (one) unit of Hanshin Type 6 LH 28 RG with 1,000 HP x 355 Rpm and equipped with 2 (two) units Auxiliary Engine i.e. Mitsui Deutz 50 HP and Yanmar Type 6 HAL - HTN 180 HP (in Engine room) and </span><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="font-size: 9pt; line-height: 18px;"><span style="font-size: 14px;">2 (two) units Emergency Generator (no data) in Boat deck.</span><span style="color: red; font-size: 14px;">&nbsp;</span><span style="font-size: 14px;">The Engine Room was located in the aft area. Main Engine, Auxiliary Engines reported in working order. &nbsp;&nbsp;</span></span></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="font-size: 9pt; line-height: 18px;"><span style="font-size: 14px;">POLLUTION</span><o:p></o:p></span></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 18px;"><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">SOPEP Equipment was found not completed</span>,&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">Bunker connection was found obstructed with foreign materials,&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">Fuel air vents were found in fair condition,&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">Fuel air vents, Bunker manifolds, Anchor windlass hydraulic operating handle, and Emergency generator (s) were found not fitted with save-alls/ drip tray,&nbsp;</span><span style="font-size: 0.875rem;">Scupper plugs were found not available, and Oil absorbent were found not available.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="font-size: 9pt; line-height: 18px;"><span style="font-size: 14px;">NAVIGATION</span><o:p></o:p></span></span></p><p></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 18px;">Navigation and communication fitted on the Bridge such Gyro Compass, Magnetic Compass, Radar, AIS, Echo Sounder, GPS, VHF Radios etc. Navigational Charts were sufficient for trading area but not updated as per last BPI and NTM / BPI was found not supplied on board regularly.</span></p>', '<p>The vessel was found in satisfactory structural condition but several items to be repaired/rectified.&nbsp; Bridge equipment was found satisfactory but NTM/ BPI to be supplied and Charts to be updated. The Crew and Ship Management are still can be improved. Pollution prevention and equipment was found satisfactory but SOPEP, Scupper plugs, Oil absorbents to be provided.&nbsp;</p>', '2026-01-20', '2027-01-20', NOW(), NOW()) ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET status = EXCLUDED.status, summary = EXCLUDED.summary;
INSERT INTO surveys (id, vessel_id, surveyor_id, broker_id, surveyor_name, condition_type, status, form_status, location, date_of_survey, due_date, concern_from_surveyor, resume_from_surveyor, summary, policy_period_start, policy_period_end, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (624, 469, 3, 9, NULL, 'Survey', 'Outstanding', 'draft', NULL, NULL, '2026-02-19', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-01-20', '2027-01-20', NOW(), NOW()) ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET status = EXCLUDED.status, summary = EXCLUDED.summary;
INSERT INTO surveys (id, vessel_id, surveyor_id, broker_id, surveyor_name, condition_type, status, form_status, location, date_of_survey, due_date, concern_from_surveyor, resume_from_surveyor, summary, policy_period_start, policy_period_end, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (625, 470, 8, 9, 'E.Prasetya Nugraha, S.T., M.T.', 'Survey', 'Completed', 'complete', 'Jetty Mirah, Tanjung Perak Port, Surabaya, East Java - Indonesia', '2026-02-28', '2026-02-14', '<p><b>STRUCTURAL COMPLIANCE WITH GENERAL MARINE INDUSTRY STANDARDS</b></p><ol><li>UTM Report was found Unavailable Onboard</li><li>Deviation Card was found not posted on bridge</li><li>Latest NTM was found Unavailable Onboard</li><li>Paper Chart was found Not Updated With Latest NTM/ BPI</li><li>Echo Sounder was found not fitted on bridge (Rectified)</li><li>Steel Save-Alls / Drip Tray was found not fitted at FO &amp; LO Vents and Bunker Manifold</li><li>Scupper Plugs were found Unavailable On Board</li><li>Oil Absorbent was found Unavailable On Board</li><li>Draught and Plimsol were found Illegible</li><li>Hull generally was found rusty at several area</li><li>Main Deck was found Rusty</li><li>Anchor Windlass Steel Foundation was found Partly Corroded</li><li>Doubler Platting was found at Several Main Deck Area</li><li>Bulwarks was found Rusty and Partly Corroded</li><li>Bollards, Rollers &amp; Fairleads were found without SWL Marking &amp; Rusty</li><li>Rubber Gasket of CH Manhole Access were found not fitted</li><li>Manhole at Forward Deck cover was found partly corroded</li><li>Several Weathertight doors were found spot rusty</li><li>Cargo Holds was found Rusty and Partly Corroded on Tween Deck and Side Shell Frames</li><li>Several Side Stanchion were found Deformed</li><li>Doubler Plating was found at several area on Cargo Hold</li><li>Hatch Coaming were found Rusty and Partly Corroded</li><li>Hatch Cover Panels were found Rusty &amp; Partly Corroded</li><li>E/R Control Panels was found without Rubber Mat Insulation</li></ol><p><br></p>', '<p style="text-align: justify; ">The Wreck Removal &amp; Oil Pollution Survey of MV âALKEN PADMAâ was conducted on 28 February 2026 while the vessel was anchored at Jetty of Mirah, Tanjung Perak Port, Surabaya Indonesia, during cargo loading operations.&nbsp;<span style="font-size: 0.875rem;">During the survey, we were accompanied and assisted by the Master, Chief Officer, Chief Engineer, and crew.</span></p><p style="text-align: justify; "><span style="font-size: 0.875rem;"><b>HULL</b></span></p><p style="text-align: justify; ">MV âALKEN PADMAâ is a 37-year-old steel single-hull general cargo vessel with principal dimensions as per shipâs particulars:</p><ol><li style="text-align: justify;">LOA: 77.82 m</li><li style="text-align: justify;">LPP: 72.20 m</li><li style="text-align: justify;">Breadth: 13.00 m</li><li style="text-align: justify;">Depth: 6.07 m</li><li style="text-align: justify;">GT: 1,484</li><li style="text-align: justify;">NT: 446</li><li style="text-align: justify;">DWT: 2,968</li></ol><p style="text-align: justify;">The vessel is registered in Surabaya and classed with Biro Klasifikasi Indonesia (BKI). She was built by YAMANAKA ZHOSEN K.K., Japan, in July 1989.&nbsp;<span style="font-size: 0.875rem;">The vessel was reported to hold valid class certificates, including Hull &amp; Machinery Class Certificate, Load Line Certificate, and relevant statutory certificates.</span></p><p style="text-align: justify; "><b>CARGO HOLDS, MAIN DECK, AND COMPARTMENT</b></p><p style="text-align: justify; ">The vessel is fitted with one (1) cargo hold and equipped with one (1) crawler crane<span style="font-size: 0.875rem;">.&nbsp;</span><span style="font-size: 0.875rem;">The cargo holds are fitted with pontoon-type hatch covers, covered with tarpaulins. The hatch covers and coaming stays were found rusty and partly corroded. The cargo</span><span style="font-size: 0.875rem;">&nbsp;hold bilge suction test and the hose test of the Hatch Cover were not conducted due to operational reasons.&nbsp;</span><span style="font-size: 0.875rem;">The visible shell plating was found rusty, partly corroded, and doubler plating at several areas. The draught, plimsol, and forward ship''s name were observed to be illegible.</span></p><p style="text-align: justify; ">During the survey, the superstructure and accommodation spaces were found satisfactory. The main deck was found to be rusty. The top plates and stanchions of the hatch coamings/coaming stays were found rusty and partly corroded. The bulwarks were found partly corroded.</p><p style="text-align: justify; "><b>NON-CARGO TANKS</b></p><p style="text-align: justify; ">The vessel is fitted with WBT 4 (P/S), one (1) CBT, one (1) fore peak tank (FPT), one (1) aft peak tank (APT).&nbsp;<span style="font-size: 0.875rem;">Ballast overflow pressure test and inspection of the internal structure of the water ballast tanks were not carried out due to operational reasons.</span></p><p style="text-align: justify; "><b>MACHINERY</b></p><p style="text-align: justify; ">The vessel is equipped with:</p><p style="text-align: justify; ">One (1) unit Hanshin Main Engine, Type 6EL32G, rated 2,000 HP at 280 RPM</p><p style="text-align: justify; ">Two (2) units Yanmar Auxiliary Engines, Type 6KFL-T, rated 2 Ã 185 HP</p><p style="text-align: justify; ">One (1) units Daily Engine (details not available), located on engine room</p><p style="text-align: justify; ">The engine room is located aft.&nbsp;<span style="font-size: 0.875rem;">The main engine and auxiliary engines were reported to be in working order.</span></p><p style="text-align: justify; "><br></p><p style="text-align: justify; "><b>POLLUTION</b></p><p style="text-align: justify; ">Bunker manifolds and fuel air vents were found in fair condition. Save-alls / drip trays were not fitted. Scupper plugs were found unavailable. Oil-absorbent materials were not available at the time of the survey.</p><p style="text-align: justify; "><b>NAVIGATION</b></p><p style="text-align: justify; ">Navigation and communication equipment fitted on the bridge includes: Gyro Compass, Magnetic Compass, Radar, AIS, GPS, and VHF radios. However, the Echosounder was found not fitted on board.&nbsp;<span style="font-size: 0.875rem;">Navigational charts were sufficient for the vesselâs trading area; however, they were not corrected up to the latest Notices to Mariners. BPI publications were reported to be regularly supplied on board.&nbsp;</span><span style="font-size: 0.875rem;">Changeover instructions for emergency steering were not posted and displayed.</span></p>', '<p>The vessel was found in fair structural condition. However, several items need to be repaired/rectified.<br></p>', '2026-01-15', '2027-01-15', NOW(), NOW()) ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET status = EXCLUDED.status, summary = EXCLUDED.summary;
INSERT INTO surveys (id, vessel_id, surveyor_id, broker_id, surveyor_name, condition_type, status, form_status, location, date_of_survey, due_date, concern_from_surveyor, resume_from_surveyor, summary, policy_period_start, policy_period_end, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (626, 95, NULL, 9, NULL, 'Survey', 'Cancelled', 'draft', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-01-10', '2027-01-10', NOW(), NOW()) ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET status = EXCLUDED.status, summary = EXCLUDED.summary;
INSERT INTO surveys (id, vessel_id, surveyor_id, broker_id, surveyor_name, condition_type, status, form_status, location, date_of_survey, due_date, concern_from_surveyor, resume_from_surveyor, summary, policy_period_start, policy_period_end, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (627, 24, 3, 9, NULL, 'Survey', 'Cancelled', 'draft', NULL, NULL, '2026-02-09', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-01-10', '2027-01-10', NOW(), NOW()) ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET status = EXCLUDED.status, summary = EXCLUDED.summary;
INSERT INTO surveys (id, vessel_id, surveyor_id, broker_id, surveyor_name, condition_type, status, form_status, location, date_of_survey, due_date, concern_from_surveyor, resume_from_surveyor, summary, policy_period_start, policy_period_end, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (628, 471, 8, 9, 'FAJAR TRIHASTYANTO KUNCORO', 'Survey', 'Completed', 'complete', 'TANJUNG PERAK ANCHORAGE, SURABAYA - INDONESIA', '2026-01-23', '2026-02-14', '<p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 26.9pt; text-indent: -17.85pt; line-height: 21px;"><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><u><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 20px;">Structural compliance with general marine industry standards</span></u></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 26.9pt; text-indent: -17.85pt; line-height: 21px;"><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-indent: -17.85pt;">- Bunker manifolds area was found messy</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 26.9pt; text-indent: -17.85pt; line-height: 21px;"><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-indent: -17.85pt;">- Hydraulic operating handle of Anchor &amp; Mooring Windlass and Aft Mooring Winch were found not fitted with save-alls</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 26.9pt; text-indent: -17.85pt; line-height: 21px;"><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-indent: -17.85pt;">-&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">FO &amp; LO air vents and sounding pipes at Main deck (S) were found not fitted with save-alls</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 26.9pt; text-indent: -17.85pt; line-height: 21px;"><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">-&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">Winch of derricks were found not fitted with save-alls</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 26.9pt; text-indent: -17.85pt; line-height: 21px;"><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">-&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">Scupper plugs were found not available</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 26.9pt; text-indent: -17.85pt; line-height: 21px;"><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">- Oil absorbent</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">s were found not available</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 26.9pt; text-indent: -17.85pt; line-height: 21px;"><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">-&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">Main deck was found rusty</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 26.9pt; text-indent: -17.85pt; line-height: 21px;"><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">-&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">Bulwark at P &amp; S was found partly corroded</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 26.9pt; text-indent: -17.85pt; line-height: 21px;"><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">-&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">Stair to flag deck was found corroded</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 26.9pt; text-indent: -17.85pt; line-height: 21px;"><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">-&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">Hatch coaming longitudinal stiffener at forward area was found corroded</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 26.9pt; text-indent: -17.85pt; line-height: 21px;"><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">- In the&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">Internal structure of forward store was found sign of water flooding about half of the store height</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 26.9pt; text-indent: -17.85pt; line-height: 21px;"><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">-&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); text-indent: 0px; font-size: 0.875rem;">Manhole cover access to forward store was found corroded.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 26.9pt; text-indent: -17.85pt; line-height: 21px;"><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); text-indent: 0px; font-size: 0.875rem;">-&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">Tank top of cargo hold was found heavy rusty</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 26.9pt; text-indent: -17.85pt; line-height: 21px;"><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">-&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">Tween deck plate was found heavy corroded</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 26.9pt; text-indent: -17.85pt; line-height: 21px;"><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">-&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">Cargo hold bilge was found not dry with cargo residue</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 26.9pt; text-indent: -17.85pt; line-height: 21px;"><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">-&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">Suction test has not been tested due to malfunction system</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 26.9pt; text-indent: -17.85pt; line-height: 21px;"><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">-&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">Hatch covers were found partly corroded</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 26.9pt; text-indent: -17.85pt; line-height: 21px;"><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">-&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">All Manhole of WBT were found cemented</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 26.9pt; text-indent: -17.85pt; line-height: 21px;"><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">-&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">Internal structure of WBT was found heavy corroded and crack</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 26.9pt; text-indent: -17.85pt; line-height: 21px;"><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><u><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 20px;">Bridge Management.<o:p></o:p></span></u></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 26.9pt; text-indent: -17.85pt; line-height: 21px;"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 20px;">Implemented by shipâs crew but still can be improved.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 26.9pt; text-indent: -17.85pt; line-height: 21px;"><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><u><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 20px;">Navigational equipment</span></u></span><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><u><span lang="IN" style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 20px;"><o:p></o:p></span></u></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 8.7pt; text-indent: -8.7pt; line-height: 21px;"><span lang="IN" style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 20px;">&nbsp;&nbsp; The&nbsp;</span><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 20px;">navigation and communication were&nbsp;</span><span lang="IN" style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 20px;">found&nbsp;</span><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 20px;">fitted</span><span lang="IN" style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 20px;">&nbsp;on board</span><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 20px;">&nbsp;and apparently in satisfactory condition, but Deviation card was found expired, NTM/ BPI was found not supplied on board and Charts were found not updated as per latest&nbsp;</span><span style="font-size: 13.3333px; text-indent: -11.6px;">NTM/ BPI, and Changeover instruction for Emergency steering was found not posted/ displayed at the bridge.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: 21px;"><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 20px;">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<u>Competent of Officers<o:p></o:p></u></span></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-indent: 7.1pt; line-height: 21px;"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 20px;">The Officer and crew appeared to be competent; all certificates complied as per STCW standard.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-indent: 7.1pt; line-height: 21px;"><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><u><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 20px;">Interassociation of Officers and Crew<o:p></o:p></span></u></span></p><p></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size: 10pt;">&nbsp;&nbsp; All crew have good cooperation during the survey.</span></p>', '<p class="MsoHeader" style="text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="line-height: 18px;">The Wreck Removal &amp; Oil Pollution&nbsp;</span><span lang="IN" tahoma",sans-serif;mso-ansi-language:in"="" style="line-height: 18px;">survey</span><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="line-height: 18px;">&nbsp;of MV. âGulf Daoudâ was conducted on 23 January 2026, whilst she was anchored at Tanjung Perak anchorage, Surabaya, Indonesia waiting for cargo loading operation. During the survey, we were accompanied/ assisted by the Chief Officer, Chief Engineer and crew.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: 21px;"><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="font-size: 9pt; line-height: 18px;"><span style="font-size: 14px;">HULL</span><o:p></o:p></span></span></p><p class="MsoListParagraph" style="margin-left: 0cm; text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="line-height: 18px;">MV. Gulf Daoud is 43 years old vessel, </span><span tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="line-height: 18px;">single hull&nbsp;</span><span lang="IN" tahoma",sans-serif;="" mso-ansi-language:in"="" style="line-height: 18px;">steel</span><span tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="line-height: 18px;">&nbsp;General Cargo with dimension </span><span style="line-height: 18px;">LPP = 67.97 m, B</span><span style="line-height: 18px;">&nbsp;</span><span style="line-height: 18px;">= 12.80 m</span><span style="line-height: 18px;">&nbsp;</span><span style="line-height: 18px;">H =&nbsp;7.20 m</span><span tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="font-size: 9pt; line-height: 18px;"><span style="font-size: 14px;">, GT 1,697 and NT 928.</span><span style="color: red; font-size: 14px;">&nbsp;</span><span style="font-size: 14px;">The Vessel was registered at Jakarta and under Classification of Biro Klasifikasi Indonesia (BKI). The vessel&nbsp;</span></span><span lang="IN" tahoma",sans-serif;="" mso-ansi-language:in"="" style="line-height: 18px;">was&nbsp;</span><span tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="font-size: 9pt; line-height: 18px;"><span style="font-size: 14px;">built by Kimura Zosen K.K, Japan</span><span style="color: red; font-size: 14px;">&nbsp;</span><span style="font-size: 14px;">in 1983.&nbsp;Reported, the vessel has a valid Class Certificate i.e: Hull</span></span><span lang="IN" tahoma",sans-serif;mso-ansi-language:in"="" style="line-height: 18px;">&nbsp;Class</span><span tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="font-size: 9pt; line-height: 18px;"><span style="font-size: 14px;">&nbsp;Certificate, Tonnage Certificate and Load Line Certificate as well as Statutory Certificates.</span><span style="color: red; font-size: 14px;">&nbsp;</span></span><span lang="IN" tahoma",sans-serif;="" mso-ansi-language:in"="" style="line-height: 18px;">The visible shell plating was found in satisfactory condition.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="line-height: 18px;">During the survey, we found that the Superstructure and accommodation space in satisfactory condition. The&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">Main deck was found rusty.&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">Bulwark at P &amp; S was found partly corroded.&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">Stair to flag deck was found corroded.&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">Hatch coaming longitudinal stiffeners at forward area was found corroded. In the&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">Internal structure of forward store was found sign of water flooding about half of the store height.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: 21px;"><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="font-size: 9pt; line-height: 18px;"><span style="font-size: 14px;">CARGO HOLDS / COMPARTMENTS</span><o:p></o:p></span></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="line-height: 18px;">The Vessel was fitted with 1 (one) Cargo Hold and 2&nbsp;(two) units Derrick&nbsp;at Aft and Forward of cargo hold.&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">Internal structure of cargo hold was found in satisfactory condition, but&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">Tank top of cargo hold was found heavy rusty and&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">Tween deck plate was found heavy corroded</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="font-size: 9pt; line-height: 18px;"><span style="font-size: 14px;">NON-CARGO TANKS:</span><o:p></o:p></span></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span lang="IN" tahoma",sans-serif;="" mso-ansi-language:in"="" style="line-height: 18px;">The&nbsp;</span><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="line-height: 18px;">V</span><span lang="IN" tahoma",sans-serif;="" mso-ansi-language:in"="" style="line-height: 18px;">essel&nbsp;</span><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="line-height: 18px;">fitted with WBT (1 â 2 (P, C &amp; S)), Fore peak and After peak Tanks.&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">All Manholes of WBT were found cemented. The&nbsp;</span><span style="font-size: 0.875rem; color: rgb(33, 37, 41); text-align: left;">Internal structure of WBT was found heavy corroded and crack.</span><span style="font-size: 0.875rem; color: rgb(33, 37, 41); text-align: left;">&nbsp;</span><span style="font-size: 0.875rem; color: rgb(33, 37, 41); text-align: left;">Ballast tanks pressure test has been carried out and was found no leakages to the cargo hold.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="font-size: 9pt; line-height: 18px;"><span style="font-size: 14px;">MACHINERY</span><o:p></o:p></span></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="line-height: 18px;">The Vessel was equipped with 1 (one) unit of Akasaka Type AH.36 with 2,100 HP x 330 Rpm and equipped with 2 (two) units Auxiliary Engine Yanmar Type 6 KFL-T with @185 HP (in Engine room) and&nbsp;</span><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="font-size: 9pt; line-height: 18px;"><span style="font-size: 14px;">2 (two) units Emergency Generator (no data) on Boat deck.</span><span style="color: red; font-size: 14px;">&nbsp;</span><span style="font-size: 14px;">The Engine Room was located in the aft area.</span></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="font-size: 9pt; line-height: 18px;"><span style="font-size: 14px;">POLLUTION</span><o:p></o:p></span></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); text-align: left;">SOPEP Locker and equipment was found available and Fuel air vents were found in fair condition. But, the Bunker manifold area was found messy.&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">Hydraulic operating handle of Anchor &amp; Mooring Windlass and Aft Mooring Winch were found not fitted with save-alls.&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">FO &amp; LO air vents and sounding pipes at Main deck (S) were found not fitted with save-alls.&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">Winch of derricks were found not fitted with save-alls. Scupper plugs and Oil absorbents were found not available on board.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="font-size: 9pt; line-height: 18px;"><span style="font-size: 14px;">NAVIGATION</span><o:p></o:p></span></span></p><p></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="line-height: 18px;">Navigation and communication fitted on the Bridge such as Gyro Compass, Magnetic Compass, Radar, AIS, Echo Sounder, GPS, VHF Radios etc. The Deviation card was found expired. Navigational Charts were sufficient for trading area but not updated as per last NTM/ BPI and NTM / BPI was found not supplied on board regularly. Changeover instructions for emergency steering was found not posted/ displayed on the bridge.</span></p>', '<p>The vessel was found in satisfactory structural condition but several items to be repaired/rectified.&nbsp; Bridge equipment was found satisfactory, but NTM/ BPI to be supplied and Charts to be updated<span style="font-size: 0.875rem;">. The Crew and Ship Management are still can be improved. Pollution prevention and equipment was found satisfactory but Scupper plugs, Oil absorbents to be provided. Save-alls on&nbsp;</span><span style="font-size: 0.875rem;">Hydraulic operating handle of&nbsp;</span><span style="font-size: 0.875rem;">Anchor &amp; Mooring Windlass and Aft Mooring Winch, Winch of derricks and FO &amp; LO air vents to be fitted</span><span style="font-size: 0.875rem; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);">&nbsp;to be fitted.</span></p>', '2026-01-15', '2027-01-15', NOW(), NOW()) ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET status = EXCLUDED.status, summary = EXCLUDED.summary;
INSERT INTO surveys (id, vessel_id, surveyor_id, broker_id, surveyor_name, condition_type, status, form_status, location, date_of_survey, due_date, concern_from_surveyor, resume_from_surveyor, summary, policy_period_start, policy_period_end, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (629, 338, 3, 9, NULL, 'Survey', 'Outstanding', 'draft', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-01-29', '2027-01-29', NOW(), NOW()) ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET status = EXCLUDED.status, summary = EXCLUDED.summary;
INSERT INTO surveys (id, vessel_id, surveyor_id, broker_id, surveyor_name, condition_type, status, form_status, location, date_of_survey, due_date, concern_from_surveyor, resume_from_surveyor, summary, policy_period_start, policy_period_end, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (630, 339, 8, 9, 'Fajar Trihastyanto Kuncoro', 'Survey', 'Completed', 'complete', 'Gresik Anchorage, Gresik - Indonesia', '2026-09-02', '2026-02-28', '<p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify;"><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><u><span lang="EN-GB">Structural compliance with general marine industry standards</span></u></span><o:p></o:p></p><ul><li style="text-align: justify;"><span style="text-align: left;">SOPEP locker and equipment were found not available</span></li><li style="text-align: justify;"><span style="text-align: left;">Bunker manifolds were found obstructed with foreign materials</span></li><li style="text-align: justify;"><span style="text-align: left;">One of fuel-oil air vent on port side main deck was found corroded and without vent head</span></li><li>Save-alls of bunker manifolds were found heavy corroded and holed</li><li>Save-alls were found not fitted at fuel-oil air vents on the port and starboard sides, hydraulic operating handle of hatch covers, aft and forward winch</li><li>Scupper plugs were found not available</li><li>Oil absorbents were found not available on board</li><li>Forward hull was found dented and crack</li><li>Hull was found oil stained on several places</li><li>Hull was found marine growth below water line</li><li>Main deck on the port and starboard side was found rusty, oily and dirty</li><li>Almost hatch coaming structure was found heavy rusty/ corroded</li><li>Hydraulic pipe of anchor winch, hatch covers and derricks were found leakages</li><li>Derrick deck was found oily</li><li>Drums of anchor winch were found heavy rusty</li><li>Forward lower deck (hydraulic pump room) was found flooded with hydraulic oil</li><li>Doubler was found fitted at aft starboard side main deck</li><li>Bulwark at forward area was found partly corroded</li><li>Weather tight door of E/R and store outside accommodation were found corroded at lower part</li><li>All weather tight door was found without Open/ Close marking</li><li>Cargo hold bilges (P & S) were found dirty with cargo residue</li><li>Hatch cover panels were found rusty</li><li>Almost Packing channels of hatch cover panels were found heavy corroded</li><li>Almost rubber gasket of hatch covers was found missing</li><li>Means of communication of engine room to bridge was found out of order</li><li>OWS overboard valve was found not secured with chain & padlock, and pollution warning notice not posted</li><li>Engine room bilge was found oily water/ sludge</li></ul><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify;"><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><u><span lang="EN-GB">Bridge Management.</span></u></span><o:p></o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify;"><span lang="EN-GB">Implemented by shipâs crew but still can be improved.</span><o:p></o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify;"><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><u><span lang="EN-GB">Navigational equipment</span></u></span><o:p></o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify;"><span style="text-align: left;">Magnetic compass was found bubble and a valid deviation card not available on board.Â </span><span style="font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">The latest Notices to Mariners (NTM) were found not available on board.Â </span><span style="font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">The nautical charts had not been corrected using the latest available Notice to Mariners (NTM).Â </span><span style="font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">Echo sounder was found not available. SSB Radio was found out of order.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify;"><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><u><span lang="EN-GB">Competent of Officers</span></u></span><o:p></o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify;"><span lang="EN-GB">The Officer and crew appeared to be competent; all certificates complied as per STCW standard.</span><o:p></o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify;"><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><u><span lang="EN-GB">Interassociation of Officers and Crew</span></u></span><o:p></o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 26.9pt; text-indent: -17.85pt; line-height: 21px;"></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify;"><span lang="EN-GB">All crew have good cooperation during the survey.</span></p>', '<p class="MsoHeader" style="text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="line-height: 18px;">The Wreck Removal & Oil Pollution </span><span lang="IN" tahoma",sans-serif;mso-ansi-language:in"="" style="line-height: 18px;">survey</span><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="line-height: 18px;"> of MV. âNithamasâ was conducted on 2 September 2026, whilst she anchored at Gresik anchorage, Gresik, Indonesia waiting for berthing schedule for cargo loading operation. During the survey, we were accompanied/ assisted by the Chief Officer, Chief Engineer and crew.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: 21px;"><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="font-size: 9pt; line-height: 18px;"><span style="font-size: 14px;">HULL</span><o:p></o:p></span></span></p><p class="MsoListParagraph" style="margin-left: 0cm; text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="line-height: 18px;">MV. Nithamas is 36 years old vessel, t</span><span lang="IN" tahoma",sans-serif;="" mso-ansi-language:in"="" style="line-height: 18px;">he </span><span tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="line-height: 18px;">vessel</span><span lang="IN" tahoma",sans-serif;mso-ansi-language:in"="" style="line-height: 18px;"> was</span><span lang="IN" tahoma",sans-serif;mso-ansi-language:en-gb"="" style="line-height: 18px;"> </span><span lang="IN" tahoma",sans-serif;="" mso-ansi-language:in"="" style="line-height: 18px;">a</span><span tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="line-height: 18px;"> double hull double bottomÂ </span><span lang="IN" tahoma",sans-serif;="" mso-ansi-language:in"="" style="line-height: 18px;">steel</span><span tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="line-height: 18px;"> General Cargo with dimension LOA = 59.40 m, LPP = 56.60 m,</span><span style="line-height: 18px;">Â B</span><span style="line-height: 18px;"> </span><span style="line-height: 18px;">= 10.50 m, H = 5.80 m</span><span tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="font-size: 9pt; line-height: 18px;"><span style="font-size: 14px;">, GT 923 and NT 539.</span><span style="color: red; font-size: 14px;"> </span><span style="font-size: 14px;">The Vessel was registered at Surabaya and under Classification of Biro Klasifikasi Indonesia (BKI). The vessel </span></span><span lang="IN" tahoma",sans-serif;="" mso-ansi-language:in"="" style="line-height: 18px;">was </span><span tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="font-size: 9pt; line-height: 18px;"><span style="font-size: 14px;">built by Yoshida Zosen Kogyo Co., Ltd., Japan</span><span style="color: red; font-size: 14px;"> </span><span style="font-size: 14px;">in 1990. Reported, the vessel has a valid Class Certificate i.e: Hull & Machinery</span></span><span lang="IN" tahoma",sans-serif;mso-ansi-language:in"="" style="line-height: 18px;"> Class</span><span tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="font-size: 9pt; line-height: 18px;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"> Certificate, Tonnage Certificate and Load Line Certificate as well as a Statutory Certificate, However, the valid class certificate and UTM Report has not been provided during the survey.</span><span style="color: red; font-size: 14px;"> </span></span><span lang="IN" tahoma",sans-serif;="" mso-ansi-language:in"="" style="line-height: 18px;">The visible shell plating was found slightly rusty, forward hull was found dented and crack, oil stained on several places, and marine growth was found at below water line.</span></p><p class="MsoListParagraph" style="margin-left: 0cm; text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span lang="IN" tahoma",sans-serif;="" mso-ansi-language:in"="" style="line-height: 18px;">During the survey,Â </span><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="font-size: 0.875rem; line-height: 18px;">the </span><span style="font-size: 0.875rem;">Superstructure and accommodation space were found satisfactory. The general condition ofÂ </span><span style="font-size: 0.875rem;">main deck was found as follows:</span></p><p class="MsoListParagraph" style="margin-left: 0cm; text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span lang="IN" tahoma",sans-serif;="" mso-ansi-language:in"="" style="line-height: 18px;"></span></p><ul><li>Main deck on the port and starboard side was found rusty, oily and dirty</li><li>Almost hatch coaming structure was found heavy rusty/ corroded</li><li>Hydraulic pipe of anchor winch, hatch covers and derricks were found leakages</li><li>Derrick deck was found oily</li><li>Drums of anchor winch were found heavy rusty</li><li>Forward lower deck (hydraulic pump room) was found flooded with hydraulic oil</li><li>Doubler was found fitted at aft starboard side main deck</li><li>Bulwark at forward area was found partly corroded</li><li>Weather tight door of E/R and store outside accommodation were found corroded at lower part</li><li>All weather tight door was found without Open/ Close marking</li></ul><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span style="font-weight: bolder; text-align: left;">CARGO HOLDS / COMPARTMENTS</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="line-height: 18px;">The Vessel was fitted with 1 (one) Cargo Hold and 2 (two) units derricks fitted in the middle of cargo hold. The </span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">Internal structure of cargo hold was found slightly rusty but in fair condition. TheÂ </span><span style="font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">Cargo hold bilges (P & S) were found dirty with cargo residue</span><span style="font-size: 0.875rem; color: rgb(33, 37, 41); text-align: left;">.Â </span><span style="font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">Suction test has been carried out and found in working order. <font color="#212529">The vessel was fitted with hatch covers folding type.Â </font></span><span style="font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">The hatch covers were covered with 3 layers tarpaulins during sailing. Considered hose test is not necessary. However, h</span><span style="font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">atch cover panels were found rusty, a</span><span style="font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">lmost Packing channels of hatch cover panels were found heavy corroded, and a</span><span style="font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">lmost rubber gasket of hatch covers was found missing.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="font-size: 9pt; line-height: 18px;"><span style="font-size: 14px;">NON-CARGO TANKS:</span><o:p></o:p></span></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span lang="IN" tahoma",sans-serif;="" mso-ansi-language:in"="" style="line-height: 18px;">The </span><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="line-height: 18px;">V</span><span lang="IN" tahoma",sans-serif;="" mso-ansi-language:in"="" style="line-height: 18px;">essel </span><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="line-height: 18px;">fitted with 6 WBT (1 â 3 (Bottom P & S) and 4 - 6 (P & S Wing tank)), Fore peak and After peak Tanks.Â </span><span style="font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">The internal structures of WBT 2 P and 2 S were found in fair condition, no sign of oil contaminations and excessive sediment.Â </span><span style="font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">Ballast tanks pressure test has been carried out and found satisfactory with no leakages to the cargo hold.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="font-size: 9pt; line-height: 18px;"><span style="font-size: 14px;">MACHINERY</span><o:p></o:p></span></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="line-height: 18px;">The Vessel was equipped with 1 (one) unit of Hanshin Type LH 26 RG with 2,100 HP x 395 Rpm and equipped with 1 (one) unit Auxiliary Engine Yanmar Type 6 HAL - HTN with 120 kW and 1 (one) unit Auxiliary Engine Mitsui Deutz type F3L912 with 28 kW (in Engine room) and 1</span><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="font-size: 9pt; line-height: 18px;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"> (one) unit Emergency Generator (no data) at 2nd deck.</span><span style="color: red; font-size: 14px;"> </span><span style="font-size: 14px;">The Engine Room was located in the aft area. Main Engine, Auxiliary Engine and Emergency generator reported in working order. However, m</span></span><span style="font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">eans of communication of engine room to bridge was found out of order. OWS overboard valve was found not secured with chain & padlock, and pollution warning notice not posted. Engine room bilges were found oily water/ sludge.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="font-size: 9pt; line-height: 18px;"><span style="font-size: 14px;">POLLUTION</span><o:p></o:p></span></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="line-height: 18px;"><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">SOPEP locker and equipment, scupper plugs, and oil absorbents were found not available. Bunker manifolds were found obstructed with foreign materials.Â </span></span><span style="font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">One of fuel-oil air vent on port side main deck was found corroded and without vent head.Â </span><span style="font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">Save-alls of bunker manifolds were found heavy corroded and holed.Â </span><span style="font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">Save-alls were found not fitted at fuel-oil air vents on the port and starboard sides, hydraulic operating handle of hatch covers, aft and forward winch.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="font-size: 9pt; line-height: 18px;"><span style="font-size: 14px;">NAVIGATION</span><o:p></o:p></span></span></p><p></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="line-height: 18px;">Navigation and communication fitted on the Bridge such Magnetic Compass, Radar, AIS, GPS, VHF Radios etc.Â </span><span style="font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">Changeover instructions for emergency steering were found posted on bridge and steering gear room. However, m</span><span style="font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">agnetic compass was found bubble and a valid deviation card not available on board.Â </span><span style="font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">The latest Notices to Mariners (NTM) were found not available on board.Â </span><span style="font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">The nautical charts had not been corrected using the latest available Notice to Mariners (NTM).Â </span><span style="font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">Echo sounder was found not available. SSB radio was found out of order.</span></p>', '<p>The vessel was found in poor condition and many items to be repaired/rectified and supplied.Â </p>', '2026-01-29', '2027-01-29', NOW(), NOW()) ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET status = EXCLUDED.status, summary = EXCLUDED.summary;
INSERT INTO surveys (id, vessel_id, surveyor_id, broker_id, surveyor_name, condition_type, status, form_status, location, date_of_survey, due_date, concern_from_surveyor, resume_from_surveyor, summary, policy_period_start, policy_period_end, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (631, 472, 8, 9, 'FAJAR TRIHASTYANTO KUNCORO', 'Survey', 'Completed', 'complete', 'SURABAYA ANCHORAGE, SURABAYA', '2026-05-31', '2026-02-28', '<p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify;"><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><u><span lang="EN-GB">Structural compliance with general marine industry standards</span></u></span><o:p></o:p></p><ul><li style="text-align: justify;">F<span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">uel air vents (P &amp; S) were found corroded</span></li><li style="text-align: justify;">S<span style="font-size: 0.875rem; color: rgb(33, 37, 41); text-align: left;">ave-alls were found not fitted at FOT air vents (P &amp; S), and Hatch covers &amp; Anchor windlass hydraulic operating handle.</span></li><li style="text-align: justify;">O<span style="font-size: 0.875rem; color: rgb(33, 37, 41); text-align: left;">il absorbents were found not available</span></li><li style="text-align: justify;">P<span style="font-size: 0.875rem; color: rgb(33, 37, 41); text-align: left;">limsoll and Draft marks were found faded</span></li><li style="text-align: justify;">Doublers were found fitted at Starboard side main deck, Forward deck, and Aft deck</li><li style="text-align: justify;">Derrick deck was found oily/ slippery due to hydraulic system leakage</li><li style="text-align: justify;">Bollards, Rollers and Fairleads were found without SWL marking and rusty</li><li style="text-align: justify;"><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); text-align: left;">Watertight doors were found without Open/ Close marking and Watertight door of store corroded at lower area</span></li><li style="text-align: justify;"><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); text-align: left;">Many doublers were found fitted at Tank top</span></li><li>Cargo holds bilge well were found rusty/ corroded</li><li>Suction test has not been conducted due to operational reasons</li><li><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41);">All inspected of Ballast tanks were found heavy rusty</span></li><li><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41);">Ballast tank pressure test has not been conducted due to operational reasons</span></li><li><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41);">Emergency generator was found in repair condition</span></li><li>Auxiliary engine no. 1 was found in repair condition</li><li>OWS was found malfunction</li><li>OWS overboard valve was found not secured with chain &amp; padlock and pollution warning notice not posted</li><li>Engine room bilge was found oily water and sludge</li></ul><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify;"><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><u><span lang="EN-GB">Bridge Management.</span></u></span><o:p></o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify;"><span lang="EN-GB">Implemented by shipâs crew but still can be improved.</span><o:p></o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify;"><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><u><span lang="EN-GB">Navigational equipment</span></u></span><o:p></o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify;"><span lang="IN">The </span><span lang="EN-US">navigation and communication were </span><span lang="IN">found </span><span lang="EN-US">fitted</span><span lang="IN"> on board</span><span lang="EN-US"> and apparently in satisfactory condition. However, </span>Echo Sounder was found not available. Deviation card was found expired (more than 2 years).&nbsp;<span lang="EN-US">NTM/ BPI was found not supplied regularly and Charts were found not corrected as per latest </span>NTM/ BPI.<o:p></o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify;"><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><u><span lang="EN-GB">Competent of Officers</span></u></span><o:p></o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify;"><span lang="EN-GB">The Officer and crew appeared to be competent; all certificates complied as per STCW standard.</span><o:p></o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify;"><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><u><span lang="EN-GB">Interassociation of Officers and Crew</span></u></span><o:p></o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 26.9pt; text-indent: -17.85pt; line-height: 21px;"></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify;"><span lang="EN-GB">All crew have good cooperation during the survey.</span></p>', '<p class="MsoHeader" style="text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="line-height: 18px;">The Wreck Removal &amp; Oil Pollution </span><span lang="IN" tahoma",sans-serif;mso-ansi-language:in"="" style="line-height: 18px;">survey</span><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="line-height: 18px;"> of MV. âSurya Papuaâ was conducted on 31 May 2026, whilst she anchored at Surabaya anchorage, Surabaya, Indonesia waiting for cargo loading operation. During the survey, we were accompanied/ assisted by the Chief Officer, Chief Engineer and crew.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: 21px;"><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="font-size: 9pt; line-height: 18px;"><span style="font-size: 14px;">HULL</span><o:p></o:p></span></span></p><p class="MsoListParagraph" style="margin-left: 0cm; text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="line-height: 18px;">MV. Surya Papua&nbsp;<span style="background-color: rgb(247, 247, 247);">is 36</span>&nbsp;years old vessel, t</span><span lang="IN" tahoma",sans-serif;="" mso-ansi-language:in"="" style="line-height: 18px;">he </span><span tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="line-height: 18px;">vessel</span><span lang="IN" tahoma",sans-serif;mso-ansi-language:in"="" style="line-height: 18px;"> was</span><span lang="IN" tahoma",sans-serif;mso-ansi-language:en-gb"="" style="line-height: 18px;"> </span><span lang="IN" tahoma",sans-serif;="" mso-ansi-language:in"="" style="line-height: 18px;">a</span><span tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="line-height: 18px;"> single hull </span><span lang="IN" tahoma",sans-serif;="" mso-ansi-language:in"="" style="line-height: 18px;">steel</span><span tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="line-height: 18px;"> General Cargo with dimension </span><span style="line-height: 18px;">LOA= 71.42, LPP = <span style="background-color: rgb(247, 247, 247);">66.14 m, B</span></span><span style="background-color: rgb(247, 247, 247);"><span style="line-height: 18px;"> </span><span style="line-height: 18px;">= 11.00 m</span><span style="line-height: 18px;"> </span><span style="line-height: 18px;">H = 6.20 m</span></span><span tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="font-size: 9pt; line-height: 18px;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="background-color: rgb(247, 247, 247);">, GT 1305 and NT 463</span>.</span><span style="color: red; font-size: 14px;"> </span><span style="font-size: 14px;">The Vessel was registered at<span style="background-color: rgb(247, 247, 247);"> Tanjung Perak and u</span>nder Classification of Biro Klasifikasi Indonesia (BKI).<span style="background-color: rgb(247, 247, 247);"> The vessel </span></span></span><span lang="IN" tahoma",sans-serif;="" mso-ansi-language:in"="" style="line-height: 18px; background-color: rgb(247, 247, 247);">was </span><span tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="font-size: 9pt; line-height: 18px;"><span style="background-color: rgb(247, 247, 247);"><span style="font-size: 14px;">built by K.K. Yoshida Zosen Kogyo, Japan</span><span style="color: red; font-size: 14px;"> </span></span><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="background-color: rgb(247, 247, 247);">in 1990.</span> Reported, the vessel has a valid Class Certificate i.e: Hull &amp; Machinery</span></span><span lang="IN" tahoma",sans-serif;mso-ansi-language:in"="" style="line-height: 18px;"> Class</span><span tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="font-size: 9pt; line-height: 18px;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"> Certificate, Tonnage Certificate and Load Line Certificate as well as a Statutory Certificate.</span><span style="color: red; font-size: 14px;"> </span></span><span lang="IN" tahoma",sans-serif;="" mso-ansi-language:in"="" style="line-height: 18px;">The visible shell plating was found slight rusty but in satisfactory condition. However,&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">Plimsoll and Draft marks were found faded.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="line-height: 18px;"><span style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);">During the survey, we found that the Main deck was found rusty but in fair condition. The Superstructure and accommodation space were found satisfactory. The deck fittings were found in fair condition.</span>&nbsp;However.&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">Doublers were found fitted at Starboard side main deck, Forward deck, and Aft deck.&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">Derrick deck was found oily/ slippery due to hydraulic system leakage.&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">Bollards, Rollers and Fairleads were found without SWL marking and rusty.&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">Watertight doors were found without Open/ Close marking and Watertight door of store corroded at lower area.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span style="font-weight: bolder; text-align: left;">CARGO HOLDS / COMPARTMENTS</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="line-height: 18px;">The Vessel was fitted with 1 (one) Cargo Hold, 2 (two) units Derrick&nbsp;at middle of cargo hold. </span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">Internal structure of cargo hold was found in satisfactory condition. However, m</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">any doublers were found fitted at Tank top.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">The </span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">Cargo </span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); text-align: left;">holds bilge well (P &amp; S) were </span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">found rusty/ corroded.&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">Suction test has not been conducted due to operational reasons.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: left; line-height: 21px;"><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41);">Hatch covers and Hatch coaming were found in fair condition.&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">Hose test has been carried out and found no leakage to the cargo holds.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="font-size: 9pt; line-height: 18px;"><span style="font-size: 14px;">NON-CARGO TANKS:</span><o:p></o:p></span></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span lang="IN" tahoma",sans-serif;="" mso-ansi-language:in"="" style="line-height: 18px;">The </span><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="line-height: 18px;">V</span><span lang="IN" tahoma",sans-serif;="" mso-ansi-language:in"="" style="line-height: 18px;">essel </span><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="line-height: 18px;">fitted with 6 WBT (1 â 3 (P &amp; S)), Fore peak and After peak Tanks.&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); text-align: left;">All inspected of Ballast tanks were found heavy rusty</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">.&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">Ballast tank pressure test has not been conducted due to operational reasons. Fore peak and After peak Tanks have not been inspected due to fully with fresh water.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="font-size: 9pt; line-height: 18px;"><span style="font-size: 14px;">MACHINERY</span><o:p></o:p></span></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="line-height: 18px;">The Vessel was equipped with 1 (one) unit of Hanshin Type LH 28 RG with 1,000 HP x 365 Rpm, equipped with 2 (two) units Auxiliary Engine i.e. Yanmar Type 6 HAL - HTN with @160 HP (in 2nd Deck and Engine room), 1 (one) unit Auxiliary engine with no data in 2nd Deck, and&nbsp;</span><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="font-size: 0.875rem; line-height: 18px;">1</span><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="font-size: 9pt; line-height: 18px;"><span style="font-size: 14px;"> (one) unit Emergency Generator (no data) in Steering Gear Room.</span><span style="color: red; font-size: 14px;"> </span><span style="font-size: 14px;">The Engine Room was located in the aft area. Main Engine reported in working order. Auxiliary Engines No. 2 &amp; No. 3 reported in working order. However,&nbsp;</span></span><span style="font-size: 0.875rem; color: rgb(33, 37, 41); text-align: left;">Auxiliary engine no. 1 was found in repair condition. E</span><span style="font-size: 0.875rem; color: rgb(33, 37, 41); text-align: left;">mergency generator was found in repair condition.&nbsp;</span><span style="font-size: 0.875rem; color: rgb(33, 37, 41); text-align: left;">OWS was found malfunction.&nbsp;</span><span style="font-size: 0.875rem; color: rgb(33, 37, 41); text-align: left;">OWS overboard valve was found not secured with chain &amp; padlock and pollution warning notice not posted.&nbsp;</span><span style="font-size: 0.875rem; color: rgb(33, 37, 41); text-align: left;">Engine room bilge was found oily water and sludge</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="font-size: 9pt; line-height: 18px;"><span style="font-size: 14px;">POLLUTION</span><o:p></o:p></span></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span style="text-align: left; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);">SOPEP locker and equipment were found available. </span><span style="font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);">Bunker manifolds were found in fair condition. </span><span style="font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);">Scupper plugs were found available. Save-alls were found fitted at Bunkering manifolds, Aft Mooring winches Hydraulic operating handle and A/ E No. 2 &amp; A/ E No. 3. However, F</span><span style="font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);">uel air vents (P &amp; S) were found corroded. </span><span style="font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);">Save-alls were found not fitted at FOT air vents (P &amp; S), and Hatch covers &amp; Anchor windlass hydraulic operating handle. </span><span style="font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);">Oil absorbents were found not available.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="font-size: 9pt; line-height: 18px;"><span style="font-size: 14px;">NAVIGATION</span><o:p></o:p></span></span></p><p></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="line-height: 18px;">Navigation and communication fitted on the Bridge such Gyro Compass, Magnetic Compass, AIS, Radar, GPS, VHF Radios etc</span><span style="font-size: 0.875rem;">. However, Echo Sounder was found not available.&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">Deviation card was found expired (more than 2 years).&nbsp;</span><span style="font-size: 0.875rem;">Navigational Charts were sufficient for trading area but not corrected as per latest NTM/ BPI and NTM / BPI was found not supplied on board regularly. The&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">Changeover instructions for emergency steering were found posted in Bahasa Indonesia.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span style="font-size: 0.875rem;"></span></p>', '<p>The vessel was found in satisfactory structural condition but several items to be repaired/rectified.&nbsp;</p>', '2026-01-29', '2027-01-29', NOW(), NOW()) ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET status = EXCLUDED.status, summary = EXCLUDED.summary;
INSERT INTO surveys (id, vessel_id, surveyor_id, broker_id, surveyor_name, condition_type, status, form_status, location, date_of_survey, due_date, concern_from_surveyor, resume_from_surveyor, summary, policy_period_start, policy_period_end, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (632, 23, 8, 9, 'FAJAR TRIHASTYANTO KUNCORO', 'Survey', 'Completed', 'complete', 'TANJUNG PERAK ANCHORAGE, SURABAYA - INDONESIA', '2026-01-24', '2026-03-31', '<p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 26.9pt; text-indent: -17.85pt; line-height: 21px;"><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><u><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 20px;">Structural compliance with general marine industry standards</span></u></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 26.9pt; text-indent: -17.85pt; line-height: 21px;"><span style="font-size: 13.3333px;">- <font color="#212529">UTM Report was found not available</font></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 26.9pt; text-indent: -17.85pt; line-height: 21px;"><span style="font-size: 13.3333px;"><font color="#212529">- Bunker manifolds area was found messy</font></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 26.9pt; text-indent: -17.85pt; line-height: 21px;"><span style="font-size: 13.3333px;"><font color="#212529">-&nbsp;</font></span><span style="font-size: 0.875rem; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);">Save-alls were found not fitted on&nbsp;</span><span style="font-size: 0.875rem; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);">FO &amp; LO air vents and sounding pipes,&nbsp;</span><span style="font-size: 0.875rem; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);">Hydraulic operating handle of Anchor &amp; Mooring Windlass and&nbsp;</span><span style="font-size: 0.875rem; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);">aft Mooring Winches.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 26.9pt; text-indent: -17.85pt; line-height: 21px;"><span style="font-size: 0.875rem; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);">- Oil absorbents were found not available.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 26.9pt; text-indent: -17.85pt; line-height: 21px;"><span style="font-size: 0.875rem; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);">- Main deck was found messy</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 26.9pt; text-indent: -17.85pt; line-height: 21px;"><span style="font-size: 0.875rem; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);">- W</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem;">atertight doors were found without Open/ Close marking</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 26.9pt; text-indent: -17.85pt; line-height: 21px;"><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><u><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 20px;">Bridge Management.<o:p></o:p></span></u></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 26.9pt; text-indent: -17.85pt; line-height: 21px;"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 20px;">Implemented by shipâs crew but still can be improved.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 26.9pt; text-indent: -17.85pt; line-height: 21px;"><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><u><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 20px;">Navigational equipment</span></u></span><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><u><span lang="IN" style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 20px;"><o:p></o:p></span></u></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-left: 8.7pt; text-indent: -8.7pt; line-height: 21px;"><span lang="IN" style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 20px;">&nbsp;&nbsp; The&nbsp;</span><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 20px;">navigation and communication were&nbsp;</span><span lang="IN" style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 20px;">found&nbsp;</span><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 20px;">fitted</span><span lang="IN" style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 20px;">&nbsp;on board</span><span lang="EN-US" style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 20px;">&nbsp;and apparently in satisfactory condition.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: 21px;"><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 20px;">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<u>Competent of Officers<o:p></o:p></u></span></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-indent: 7.1pt; line-height: 21px;"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 20px;">The Officer and crew appeared to be competent; all certificates complied as per STCW standard.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-indent: 7.1pt; line-height: 21px;"><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><u><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 20px;">Interassociation of Officers and Crew<o:p></o:p></span></u></span></p><p></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size: 10pt;">&nbsp;&nbsp; All crew have good cooperation during the survey.</span></p>', '<p class="MsoHeader" style="text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="line-height: 18px;">The Wreck Removal &amp; Oil Pollution&nbsp;</span><span lang="IN" tahoma",sans-serif;mso-ansi-language:in"="" style="line-height: 18px;">survey</span><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="line-height: 18px;">&nbsp;of MV. âSamudra Prima Iâ was conducted on 24 January 2026, whilst she anchored at Tanjung perak anchorage, Surabaya, Indonesia waiting for cargo loading operation. During the survey, we were accompanied/ assisted by the Chief Officer, Chief Engineer and crew.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: 21px;"><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="font-size: 9pt; line-height: 18px;"><span style="font-size: 14px;">HULL</span><o:p></o:p></span></span></p><p class="MsoListParagraph" style="margin-left: 0cm; text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="line-height: 18px;">MV. Samudra Prima I&nbsp;is 37 years old vessel, t</span><span lang="IN" tahoma",sans-serif;="" mso-ansi-language:in"="" style="line-height: 18px;">he&nbsp;</span><span tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="line-height: 18px;">vessel</span><span lang="IN" tahoma",sans-serif;mso-ansi-language:in"="" style="line-height: 18px;">&nbsp;was</span><span lang="IN" tahoma",sans-serif;mso-ansi-language:en-gb"="" style="line-height: 18px;">&nbsp;</span><span lang="IN" tahoma",sans-serif;="" mso-ansi-language:in"="" style="line-height: 18px;">a</span><span tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="line-height: 18px;">&nbsp;single hull&nbsp;</span><span lang="IN" tahoma",sans-serif;="" mso-ansi-language:in"="" style="line-height: 18px;">steel</span><span tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="line-height: 18px;">&nbsp;General Cargo with dimension </span><span style="line-height: 18px;">LPP = 70.50 m, B</span><span style="line-height: 18px;">&nbsp;</span><span style="line-height: 18px;">= 12.50 m, H = 7.00 m</span><span tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="font-size: 9pt; line-height: 18px;"><span style="font-size: 14px;">, GT 1486 and NT 529.</span><span style="color: red; font-size: 14px;">&nbsp;</span><span style="font-size: 14px;">The Vessel was registered at Surabaya and under Classification of Biro Klasifikasi Indonesia (BKI). The vessel&nbsp;</span></span><span lang="IN" tahoma",sans-serif;="" mso-ansi-language:in"="" style="line-height: 18px;">was&nbsp;</span><span tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="font-size: 9pt; line-height: 18px;"><span style="font-size: 14px;">built by K.K Miura Zosenho, Japan</span><span style="color: red; font-size: 14px;">&nbsp;</span><span style="font-size: 14px;">in 1989.&nbsp;Reported, the vessel has a valid Class Certificate i.e: Hull &amp; Machinery</span></span><span lang="IN" tahoma",sans-serif;mso-ansi-language:in"="" style="line-height: 18px;">&nbsp;Class</span><span tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="font-size: 9pt; line-height: 18px;"><span style="font-size: 14px;">&nbsp;Certificate, Tonnage Certificate and Load Line Certificate as well as a Statutory Certificate.</span><span style="color: red; font-size: 14px;">&nbsp;</span></span><span lang="IN" tahoma",sans-serif;="" mso-ansi-language:in"="" style="line-height: 18px;">The visible shell plating was found in good condition and well coating.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="line-height: 18px;">During the survey, we found that the&nbsp;</span><span style="font-size: 0.875rem;">Superstructure and accommodation space were found satisfactory. But&nbsp;</span><span style="font-size: 0.875rem;">Main deck was found messy and Watertight doors were found without Open/ Close marking.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="line-height: 21px;"><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="font-size: 9pt; line-height: 18px;"><span style="font-size: 14px;">CARGO HOLDS / COMPARTMENTS</span><o:p></o:p></span></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="line-height: 18px;">The Vessel was fitted with 1 (one) Cargo Hold. The&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">Internal structure of cargo hold was found in fair condition. The&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">Cargo hold bilges was found in fair condition and clean. Suction test has been carried out and found satisfactory. The vessel was not fitted with&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">Hatch covers and rubber sealing (not applicable). Hose test not applicable.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="font-size: 9pt; line-height: 18px;"><span style="font-size: 14px;">NON-CARGO TANKS:</span><o:p></o:p></span></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span lang="IN" tahoma",sans-serif;="" mso-ansi-language:in"="" style="line-height: 18px;">The&nbsp;</span><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="line-height: 18px;">V</span><span lang="IN" tahoma",sans-serif;="" mso-ansi-language:in"="" style="line-height: 18px;">essel&nbsp;</span><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="line-height: 18px;">fitted with 6 WBT (1 â 3 (Bottom P &amp; S) and 4 - 6 (P &amp; S Wing tank)), Fore peak and After peak Tanks. The&nbsp;<span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); text-align: left;">Internal structures of WBT were found in satisfactory condition</span>.&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">Ballast tank pressure test has been carried out and found satisfactory.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="font-size: 9pt; line-height: 18px;"><span style="font-size: 14px;">MACHINERY</span><o:p></o:p></span></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="line-height: 18px;">The Vessel was equipped with 1 (one) unit of Niigata Type 6 M 31 AFTE with 1,800 HP x 360 Rpm and equipped with 1 (one) unit Auxiliary Engine Yanmar Type 6 HAL - N 160 HP (in Engine room) and 1</span><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="font-size: 9pt; line-height: 18px;"><span style="font-size: 14px;">&nbsp;(one) unit Emergency Generator (no data) on forward store.</span><span style="color: red; font-size: 14px;">&nbsp;</span><span style="font-size: 14px;">The Engine Room was located in the aft area. Main Engine, Auxiliary Engine and Emergency generator reported in working order. &nbsp;&nbsp;</span></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="font-size: 9pt; line-height: 18px;"><span style="font-size: 14px;">POLLUTION</span><o:p></o:p></span></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="line-height: 18px;"><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">SOPEP Equipment was found satisfactory.&nbsp;</span></span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">Fuel air vents were found in fair condition. Scupper plugs were found available. But&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">Bunker manifolds area was found messy. Save-alls were found not fitted on&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">FO &amp; LO air vents and sounding pipes,&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">Hydraulic operating handle of Anchor &amp; Mooring Windlass and&nbsp;</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">aft Mooring Winches. Oil absorbents were found not available.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="font-size: 9pt; line-height: 18px;"><span style="font-size: 14px;">NAVIGATION</span><o:p></o:p></span></span></p><p></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify; line-height: 21px;"><span lang="EN-US" tahoma",sans-serif"="" style="line-height: 18px;">Navigation and communication fitted on the Bridge such Gyro Compass, Magnetic Compass, Radar, AIS, Echo Sounder, GPS, VHF Radios etc. Navigational Charts were sufficient for trading area and updated as per last BPI and NTM / BPI was found supplied on board regularly. C</span><span style="color: rgb(33, 37, 41); font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: left;">hangeover instructions for Emergency Steering were found posted/ displayed.</span></p>', '<p>The vessel was found in satisfactory structural condition but several items to be repaired/rectified. Save-alls to be fitted on&nbsp;<span style="font-size: 0.875rem; text-indent: -23.8px; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);">FO &amp; LO air vents and sounding pipes,&nbsp;</span><span style="font-size: 0.875rem; text-indent: -23.8px; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);">Hydraulic operating handle of Anchor &amp; Mooring Windlass and&nbsp;</span><span style="font-size: 0.875rem; text-indent: -23.8px; color: rgb(33, 37, 41);">aft Mooring Winches. Oil absorbent to be provided. Main deck and bunker manifolds area to be tidied.</span></p>', '2026-03-01', '2027-03-01', NOW(), NOW()) ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET status = EXCLUDED.status, summary = EXCLUDED.summary;
INSERT INTO surveys (id, vessel_id, surveyor_id, broker_id, surveyor_name, condition_type, status, form_status, location, date_of_survey, due_date, concern_from_surveyor, resume_from_surveyor, summary, policy_period_start, policy_period_end, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (633, 473, 8, 9, 'Erriawan Dharma Santosa', 'Survey', 'Completed', 'complete', 'GRESIK ANCHORAGE', '2026-02-25', '2026-02-21', '<p class="MsoNormal"><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><u>Structural compliance with general marine industry standards</u></span><o:p></o:p></p><p style="margin-bottom: 0cm; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18pt; line-height: 21px;"><span style="font-family: Symbol;">Â·<span times="" new="" roman";"="" style="font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-language-override: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal;">&nbsp; &nbsp;</span></span></p><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle" style="margin-left:18.0pt;mso-add-space:nauto;text-indent:-18.0pt;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1"><span style="text-indent: -18pt; font-size: 0.875rem;">-&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Deviation card was found latest adjusted on 28nMay 2021 (more than 2 years)</span></p>nn<p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle" style="margin-left:18.0pt;mso-add-space:nauto;text-indent:-18.0pt;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1"><!--[if !supportLists]-->-<span style="font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-language-override: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: " times="" new="" roman";"="">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;n</span><!--[endif]-->Display of Echo sounder display was found notnclear (malfunction)<span style="font-size: 10.5pt; line-height: 115%; color: rgb(33, 37, 41); background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;"> </span><o:p></o:p></p>nn<p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle" style="margin-left:18.0pt;mso-add-space:nauto;text-indent:-18.0pt;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1"><!--[if !supportLists]-->-<span style="font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-language-override: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: " times="" new="" roman";"="">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;n</span><!--[endif]-->Change over instruction for emergency steeringnwas found not posted<o:p></o:p></p>nn<p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle" style="margin-left:18.0pt;mso-add-space:nauto;text-indent:-18.0pt;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1"><!--[if !supportLists]-->-<span style="font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-language-override: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: " times="" new="" roman";"="">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;n</span><!--[endif]-->Change over instruction for emergency steeringnwas found not posted<o:p></o:p></p>nn<p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle" style="margin-left:18.0pt;mso-add-space:nauto;text-indent:-18.0pt;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1"><!--[if !supportLists]-->-<span style="font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-language-override: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: " times="" new="" roman";"="">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;n</span><!--[endif]-->Scupper plugs were found not available on board<o:p></o:p></p>nn<p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle" style="margin-left:18.0pt;mso-add-space:nauto;text-indent:-18.0pt;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1"><!--[if !supportLists]-->-<span style="font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-language-override: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: " times="" new="" roman";"="">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;n</span><!--[endif]-->Oil Absorbents were found not available on board<o:p></o:p></p>nn<p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle" style="margin-left:18.0pt;mso-add-space:nauto;text-indent:-18.0pt;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1"><!--[if !supportLists]-->-<span style="font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-language-override: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: " times="" new="" roman";"="">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;n</span><!--[endif]-->Draught and Plimsoll marks were found faded/ illegible<o:p></o:p></p>nn<p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle" style="margin-left:18.0pt;mso-add-space:nauto;text-indent:-18.0pt;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1"><!--[if !supportLists]-->-<span style="font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-language-override: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: " times="" new="" roman";"="">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;n</span><!--[endif]-->Doublers were found on Main deck<o:p></o:p></p>nn<p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle" style="margin-left:18.0pt;mso-add-space:nauto;text-indent:-18.0pt;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1"><!--[if !supportLists]-->-<span style="font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-language-override: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: " times="" new="" roman";"="">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;n</span><!--[endif]-->Main deck/ gangway starboard side was foundnobstructed<o:p></o:p></p>nn<p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle" style="margin-left:18.0pt;mso-add-space:nauto;text-indent:-18.0pt;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1"><!--[if !supportLists]-->-<span style="font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-language-override: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: " times="" new="" roman";"="">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;n</span><!--[endif]-->Watertight doors were found corroded, rubbernsealing hardened and without open/ close markings<o:p></o:p></p>nn<p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle" style="margin-left:18.0pt;mso-add-space:nauto;text-indent:-18.0pt;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1"><!--[if !supportLists]-->-<span style="font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-language-override: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: " times="" new="" roman";"="">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;n</span><!--[endif]-->Tank top has not been inspected was due toncovered with wooden sheating<o:p></o:p></p>nn<p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle" style="margin-left:18.0pt;mso-add-space:nauto;text-indent:-18.0pt;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1"><!--[if !supportLists]-->-<span style="font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-language-override: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: " times="" new="" roman";"="">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;n</span><!--[endif]-->Cargo hold bilges were found dirty and remainingnwater<o:p></o:p></p>nn<p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle" style="margin-left:18.0pt;mso-add-space:nauto;text-indent:-18.0pt;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1"><!--[if !supportLists]-->-<span style="font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-language-override: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: " times="" new="" roman";"="">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;n</span><!--[endif]-->Suction test of cargo hold bilges has not beenncarried out due to operational reasons<o:p></o:p></p>nn<p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpLast" style="margin-left:18.0pt;mso-add-space:auto;ntext-indent:-18.0pt;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1"><!--[if !supportLists]-->-<span style="font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-language-override: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: " times="" new="" roman";"="">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;n</span><!--[endif]-->Tightness test of Hatch covers has not beenncarried out due to operational reasons<o:p></o:p></p><p style="margin-bottom: 0cm; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18pt; line-height: 21px;"><span style="font-size: 0.875rem; text-indent: -18pt;"><br></span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><u>Bridge Management.<o:p></o:p></u></span></p><p style="margin-bottom: 0cm; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18pt; line-height: 21px;"></p><p class="MsoNormal">Implemented by shipâs crew but still can be improved.</p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><u>Navigational equipment<o:p></o:p></u></span></p><p class="MsoNormal"></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify;">The navigation and communication were found fitted on board and apparently in satisfactory condition. NTM/ BPI was supplied on board regularly and Charts were found updated as per latest NTM/ BPI. Echo Sounder display was found not clear/ malfunction. The Changeover instructions from emergency steering was found not posted / displayed.</p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><u>Competent of Officers</u></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align: justify;"></p><p class="MsoNormal">The Officer and crew appeared to be competent; all certificates complied as per STCW standard.</p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="font-weight: bolder;"><u>Interassociation of Officers and Crew<o:p></o:p></u></span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><o:p></o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal">&nbsp;All crew have good cooperation during the survey.</p>', '<p>The Wreck Removal &amp; Oil Pollution survey of MV. âTrijaya Lestariâ was conducted on 25 February 2026, whilst she anchored at Gresik anchorage, East Java, Indonesia waiting for cargo loading operation. During the survey, we were accompanied/ assisted by the Chief Officer, Chief Engineer and crew.</p><p>HULL</p><p style="text-align: justify;">MV. Trijaya Lestari is 38 years old vessel, the vessel was a single hull steel General Dry Cargo Ship with dimension LOA = 71.50 m, B = 11.00 m Max draught = 5.20 m, GT 1244 and NT 439. The Vessel was built at Takasago Zosensho Co., Ltd., Japan in 1998, registered at Tanjung Perak, Surabaya and under Classification of Biro Klasifikasi Indonesia (BKI). T<span style="font-size: 0.875rem;">he vessel''s Class Certificates was found date of expired on&nbsp; 20 September 2029.</span></p><p style="text-align: justify;">The visible shell plating was found in satisfactory condition. The Draught and Plimsoll marks were found faded/ illegible.</p><p style="text-align: justify;">During the survey, we found that the Superstructure and accommodation space were found satisfactory. The Main deck was found in satisfcatory but several doublers were found on Main deck and starboard side gangway was found obstructed. Ship''s railing throughout the vessel was found in satisfactory condition. The bollards and roller structure were found in fair condition. The mooring ropes were found in fair condition. The fuel vents were found not fitted with save-alls. Scupper plugs and oil absorbents were found not available onboard.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>CARGO HOLDS / COMPARTMENTS</p><p style="text-align: justify;"><span style="font-size: 0.875rem;">The Vessel was fitted with 1 (one) Cargo Hold and 1 (one) unit Crawler Crane at Middle of cargo hold. Internal structure of cargo hold generally in fair condition, but the Tank top has not been inspected due to it was covered with wooden sheating. The bilge was found dirty and remaing water.&nbsp;Suction test of the bilges has not been carried out due to operational reasons.&nbsp; Hatch coaming was found in fair condition. Generally, the h</span><span style="font-size: 0.875rem;">atch covers panel was found in fair condition but hose test to the hatch covers has not been carried out due to operational reasons.&nbsp; &nbsp;</span></p><p>NON-CARGO TANKS:</p><p><span style="font-size: 0.875rem;">The Vessel fitted with 10 WBT (1 â 5 (P &amp; S)), Fore peak and After peak Tanks. Internal structure of WBT no.1, 2 and 3 P&amp;S has been inspected and found&nbsp; the internal structures was found rusty and partly corroded. The ballast tanks pressure test has not been carried out due to operational reasons.</span></p><p>MACHINERY</p><p>The Vessel was equipped with 1 (one) unit of Engine Diesel of Hanshin 6 LH 32 Gwith 1000 HP&nbsp; and equipped with 1 (one) unit Auxiliary Engines Yanmar 6 HAL - H, 150 HP and 2 (two) units Emergency Generator (no data) in the Steering gear room and Aft deck. The Engine Room was located in the aft area. Main Engine and Auxiliary Engines reported in working order.&nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>POLLUTION</p><p>Bunker Connections were found in fair condition and fitted with drip tray. However, the fuel air vents were not fitted with save-alls. The SOPEP was found available on board. Scupper plugs and Oil Absorbents were found not available on board.&nbsp;</p><p>NAVIGATION</p><p>Navigation and communication fitted on the Bridge such as Magnetic Compass, Radar, AIS, GPS, VHF Radios etc., but Echo sounder display was found not clear/ malfunction. Navigational Charts were sufficient for the vessel''s trading area and updated as per latest BPI.&nbsp; Changeover instructions from emergency steering were found not posted / displayed.</p>', '<p>The vessel MV. Trijaya Lestari was found generally in fair condition. However, the deficiency items need to be rectified.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>', '2026-01-22', '2027-01-22', NOW(), NOW()) ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET status = EXCLUDED.status, summary = EXCLUDED.summary;
INSERT INTO surveys (id, vessel_id, surveyor_id, broker_id, surveyor_name, condition_type, status, form_status, location, date_of_survey, due_date, concern_from_surveyor, resume_from_surveyor, summary, policy_period_start, policy_period_end, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (634, 64, 8, 9, 'E.Prasetya Nugraha, S.T., M.T.', 'Survey', 'Completed', 'complete', 'TANJUNG PERAK ANCHORAGE', '2026-03-01', '2026-02-28', '<p><b><u>STRUCTURAL COMPLIANCE WITH GENERAL MARINE INDUSTRY STANDARDS</u></b></p><ol style="margin-top:0cm" start="1" type="1">rn <li class="MsoNormal">The deviation card was found not posted onrn     bridge<o:p></o:p></li>rn <li class="MsoNormal">Latest NTM/BPI was found unavailable onrn     board<o:p></o:p></li>rn <li class="MsoNormal">Paper chart was found not updated withrn     latest NTM/BPI<o:p></o:p></li>rn <li class="MsoNormal">SOPEP was found insufficient equipment<o:p></o:p></li>rn <li class="MsoNormal">Bunker connection was found rusty<o:p></o:p></li>rn <li class="MsoNormal">Steel save-alls were found not fitted at FOrn     & LO vents<o:p></o:p></li>rn <li class="MsoNormal">Scupper plugs were found unavailable onrn     board<o:p></o:p></li>rn <li class="MsoNormal">Oil absorbent was found unavailable onrn     board<o:p></o:p></li>rn <li class="MsoNormal">Main deck was found rusty<o:p></o:p></li>rn <li class="MsoNormal">Forward rollers portside was found partlyrn     missing<o:p></o:p></li>rn <li class="MsoNormal">Stanchion on main deck were found spotrn     rusty<o:p></o:p></li>rn <li class="MsoNormal">Rubber gasket of CH manholes access wasrn     found not fitted<o:p></o:p></li>rn <li class="MsoNormal">Air vent of WBT were found wastage<o:p></o:p></li>rn <li class="MsoNormal">Several weathertight doors were foundrn     rusty and partly corroded<o:p></o:p></li>rn <li class="MsoNormal">Cargo holds were found rusty and partlyrn     corroded<o:p></o:p></li>rn <li class="MsoNormal">Hatch coaming/coaming stays were foundrn     rusty and partly corroded<o:p></o:p></li>rn <li class="MsoNormal">Hatch cover panels were found rusty andrn     partly corroded<o:p></o:p></li>rn <li class="MsoNormal">Hatch cover was found not to be weatherrn     tight<o:p></o:p></li>rn <li class="MsoNormal">Internal structure of ballast tankrn     inspection has not been carried out due to manhole bolting were foundrn     broken<o:p></o:p></li>rn <li class="MsoNormal">Manhole of WBT no. 2 stbd was foundrn     broken/ leakage during ballast tank pressure test<o:p></o:p></li>rn <li class="MsoNormal">Air vent of WBT no. 1 stbd was found pipern     leakage on main deck<o:p></o:p></li>rn <li class="MsoNormal">E/R control panels was found withoutrn     rubber mat insulation<o:p></o:p></li>rn</ol>', '<p style="text-align: justify; ">The Wreck Removal &amp; Oil Pollution Survey of MV. âPERSADA 88â was conducted on 01 MARCH 2026, whilst she was anchored at Tanjung Perak anchorage, East Java, Indonesia for waiting new Master due to Ex-Ship''s Master had been sign-off. During the survey, we were accompanied/ assisted by the PIC, Chief Officer, Chief Engineer, and Crew.</p><p style="text-align: justify; "><b>HULL</b></p><p style="text-align: justify; ">MV. PERSADA 88 is 35 years old vessel, the vessel was a Steel Single Hull General Cargo with dimension as per Ship particular is LOA = 89.20 m, LPP = 77.20 m, B = 13.00 m, H = 6.65 m, GT 1,964, NT 1,137, and 2,035 DWT. The Vessel was registered at Surabaya and under the classification of Biro Klasifikasi Indonesia (BKI). The vessel was built by ESBJERG S/V - DENMARK in June 1991. Reported, the vessel has a valid Class Certificate i.e: Hull &amp; Machinery Class Certificate, and Load Line Certificate as well as a Statutory Certificate.&nbsp;</p><p style="text-align: justify; ">During the survey, we found that the Superstructure and accommodation space were found satisfactory. The Main Deck was found Rusty. Forward Rollers at Portside was found partly missing,&nbsp; Stanchions on main deck were found spot rusty, rubber gasket of CH Manholes were found not fitted, Air Vent of WBT were found wastage, Several weathertight doors were found rusty and partly corroded.</p><p style="text-align: justify; "><b>CARGO HOLDS / COMPARTMENTS</b></p><p style="text-align: justify; ">The Vessel was fitted with 1 (one) Cargo Hold and equipped with 2 (two) units Deck crane. The Tanktop of Cargo Hold was found Rusty and Partly Corroded. The Cargo Hold was fitted by Pontoon Type Hatch Cover which found rusty and leakage. Hose test to the hatch covers has not been carried out due to reported by PIC and Chief Officer, that the hatch cover panel was found not weathertight conditions.</p><p style="text-align: justify; "><b>NON-CARGO TANKS</b></p><p style="text-align: justify; ">The Vessel fitted with 4 WBT (P/S), 2 WBT (C) ex FO Tank with manually pump system, Fore peak and After peak Tanks. The Internal structures of WBT had not been inspected due to broken manhole bolting.&nbsp;</p><p style="text-align: justify; "><b>MACHINERY</b></p><p style="text-align: justify; ">The Vessel was equipped with 1 (one) unit of DEUTZ MWM Type SBMV8M-628 with 1,997 HP x 900 Rpm and equipped with 2 (two) units Auxiliary Engine DEUTZ MWM Type TBD-234-V08, 2 x 258 HP (in the engine room), and 2 (two) units of the Emergency Generator (no data) at the forward deck room and at the boat deck. The Engine Room was located in the aft area. The main engine and Auxiliary Engine were reported in working order.&nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p style="text-align: justify; "><b>POLLUTION</b></p><p style="text-align: justify; ">Bunker manifolds and Fuel air vents were found in fair condition. But the Save-alls/ Drip tray was found not fitted on FO, and LO Vents. Scupper plugs were found unavailable. SOPEP Locker was found to be insufficient. Oil absorbents were found not available.</p><p style="text-align: justify; "><b>NAVIGATION</b></p><p style="text-align: justify; ">Navigation and communication fitted on the Bridge such Gyro Compass, Magnetic Compass, Radar, AIS, GPS, VHF Radios etc. However; Deviation card was not posted on bridge. Navigational Charts were sufficient for trading area but not corrected as per last BPI and Latest NTM / BPI was found unavailable onboard. Changeover instructions for Emergency Steering were found posted/ displayed.</p>', '<p class="MsoNormal"><span lang="EN-US">The vessel was found in fair structuralrncondition. However, several items need to be repaired/rectified.<o:p></o:p></span></p>', '2026-01-29', '2027-01-29', NOW(), NOW()) ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET status = EXCLUDED.status, summary = EXCLUDED.summary;
